reof along with the response received from PRIs in this regard;  \n(d) whether the complaints of violation of consumer rights increased in the country during each of \nthe last three years and the current year; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons for the same along with the action taken/being \ntaken on such complaints, State/UT-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k jkT; ea=h  \n¼Jh nkuos jkolkgsc nknkjko½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO) \n \n(a)      :  Yes, Sir. The Government carries out a multi-media “ Jago Grahak  Jago” campaign on \npan-India basis covering both rural and urban areas through print, electronic, outdoor and social media. \nConsumer Awareness information has been disseminated through post o ffices and Krishi Vigyan \nKendras.  Grants-in-aid are released to States/UTs for creating consumer awareness in the respective \nStates/UTs in their regional languages so as to further ensure that the campaign reaches the rural and \nbackward areas of the country.  Consumer awareness and education is also promoted through fairs and \nmelas in rural and urban areas.  \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n(b)  & (c) :       The Government has involved of PRIs in rural areas through Ministry of Panchayati \nRaj for effective implementation to educat e and make consumers aware about their rights across the \ncountry. As outreach efforts, the Ministry of Panchayati Raj disseminated consumer awareness \ninformation to Gram Panchayats and on the National Consumer Day on 24.12.2020, there was an \ninteraction with the selected Panchayats of Jharkhand. \n \n(d) & (e)   :       Details of consumer cases Filed, Disposed and Cumulative Pendency in all Consumer \nCommissions across the Country (State/UT-wise) during the year 2018-21 is given at Annexure. \n  \n*****  \n\n \nANNEXURE \n  \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (d) &  (e) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED