untries are likely to be provided these\nvaccines as gift; and\n(e) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN]\n(a)  As per the information available with Ministry of External Affairs, as on\n20 January 2021, around 39 lakh people have returned to India under 9\nphases of the Vande Bharat Mission. Since most Indian nationals stranded in\nforeign  countries  have  safely  returned  to  their  homes,  the  incoming\npassengers are now being treated as ‘International Arrivals’. A country-wise\nlist is attached at Annexure A.\n(b) Ministry of Health & Family Welfare and Ministry of Home Affairs\nhave been issuing revised guidelines on screening and quarantine from\ntime to time. Based on these guidelines, State Governments have been\nissuing  their  own  SOPs  for  arriving  passengers  for  the  purpose  of\nscreening, testing and quarantine.\n(c) to (e) As on 22 January 2021, India has provided Covid-19 vaccines in\nform of grant-in-aid to following countries:\n Sl. \nNo. Countries Doses\n1 Bhutan 1.5 lakh\n2 Maldives 1 lakh\n3 Bangladesh 20 lakh\n4 Nepal 10 lakh\n5 Myanmar 15 lakh\n1\n\n6 Mauritius 1 lakh\n7 Seychelles 50,000\n2\n\nAnnexure- I to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 334\nCountry wise Number of Repatriated Indians upto 20.01.2021\nCOUNTRY WISE NUMBER OF REPATRIATED INDIANS TILL\n20.01.2021\nCOUNTRY NO. OF REPATRIATED INDIANS\nAFGHANISTAN 15603\nALGERIA 1338\nANGOLA 770\nARMENIA 720\nAUSTRALIA 12593\nAZERBAIJAN 186\nBAHRAIN 56532\nBANGLADESH 26560\nBARBADOS 115\nBELARUS 232\nBELGIUM 296\nBHUTAN 1801\nBRAZIL 510\nBRUNEI 408\nBULGARIA 698\nCAMBODIA 596\nCANADA 61504\nCHINA 1257\nCROATIA 3\nDENMARK 52\nDJIBOUTI 326\nEGYPT 1892\nESTONIA 6\nETHIOPIA 11274\nFIJI 5\nFINLAND 223\nFRANCE 54246\nGEORGIA 2047\nGERMANY 65260\nGHANA 302\nGREECE 163\nHONG KONG 2248\nHUNGARY 3\nINDONESIA 4026\nIRAN 5332\nIRAQ 12412\nIRELAND 485\nISRAEL 1105\nITALY 9647\nJAPAN 9290\nJORDAN 838\nKAZAKHSTAN 3686\n