���� �\n�������������������������������������������������������������� �����������������\n�������������������������������������������������������� �������� �������������\n������������ �� �������� ��� ���� ����� ��������� ��� ������������ ������� ������\n��������� ���� ������ ����� ��������� �� �������� �������� ������ ���� �����������\n������������������������ �� ������������������������������� ����� ����������\n������� �� ��������� ���������� ����������� ����� �� ����� ���� �� �������\n������������������������������������ ������������� ��� ����������� ��������������\n����� ���������� � ��� ����� � ������ �������� ���� ��������� ��� �������������\n��������������������������������������� �\n�\n��� � ��� ������ ��� ��������� ��������� ����� ���� �� ������ �������� ���� �����\n�������� ����������������������������\n������ ������������������������������������ ��� ���� �\n������ ������������������������������������ ���� �\n���� ����������� ��� ����� � ��� ���������� ��� ������ ��� ������ ����\n��������������������� �����������������������������\n��������������� ������������������������������������ �\n�������������������������������������������� �\n�\n���� �\n�\n�\n\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |292", "t": "Public Welfare Schemes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.292 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n  \nPUBLIC WELFARE SCHEMES \n  \n292.  SHRI KUNWAR PUSHPENDRA SINGH CHANDEL: \n         SHRIMATI MALA RAJYA LAXMI SHAH: \n        \n           \nWill the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state: \n  \n(a)  whether Government has carried out changes in the funds \nallocated to various schemes and allocated more funds to the public \nwelfare schemes on priority basis due to corona pandemic; \n  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n  \n(c) the State -wise details of the beneficiaries who have benefitted \nfrom the public welfare schemes in the country including \nBundelkhand and Uttarakhand during the last one year? \n  \n  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY \nOF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION AND \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY \nOF PLANNING (RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n  \n(a) & (b)   Ministry of Statistics and Programme Impl ementation \ndeals with the MPLAD Scheme. The objective of the scheme is to \nenable Members of Parliament (MP) to recommend works of \ndevelopmental nature with emphasis  on the creation of durable \ncommunity assets based on the locally felt needs to be taken up in \ntheir Constituencies /eligible areas. Right from inception of the \n\nScheme, durable assets of national priorities viz. drinking water, \nprimary education, public health, sanitation and roads, etc. are \nbeing created. In a way, the scheme is based on the par ticipation \nof citizens in identifying the gaps needed to provide assets which \ncan further the aspirations and developmental requirements of the \ncommunity. Such requirements are expressed through the public \nrepresentatives and form the basis of the scheme. \n  \nMPLADS is not an individual beneficiary-oriented scheme. \n  \nRelease of funds under MPLADS is made on Constituency basis \nwith no geographical or regional bias. \n  \nIt may be appreciated that managing and addressing the \nchallenges faced by the nation on accou nt of COVID-19 pandemic, \nrequires pooling of all available physical, financial, medical, \ntechnological and other resources.  Accordingly, the budgetary \noutlay for FY 2020 -21 in respect of the MPLAD scheme has been \nplaced at the disposal of Ministry of Fina nce for managing the \neconomic and health impacts of COVID-19 pandemic, in pursuance \nof the decision of the Union Cabinet for not operating the MPLAD \nScheme for FY2020-21 and 2021-22. \n  \nThe annual entitlement under MPLADS remains unchanged and at \npresent, t here is no proposal to revise the annual entitlement \nunder MPLADS. \n  \n(c)     In view of (a) & (b) above, need for reply to this sub -part, \ndoes not arise. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |293", "t": "Renting of Railway Stations", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 293 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nRENTING OF RAILWAY STATIONS \n \n† 293. SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways is considering on a proposal to rent out \nthe least busy stations for the purpose of marriage \nceremonies and other programmes; \n(b) if so, whether any final decision has been taken in this regard; \nand \n(c) the manner in which Railway Stations are  likely to be \nselected to organise these ceremonies along with the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) No, Sir. \n \n(b) & (c): Do not arise. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |294", "t": "Unmanned Level Crossings", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.294 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nUNMANNED LEVEL CROSSINGS \n294.  SHRI MAHESH SAHOO: \n       SHRI BIDYUT BARAN MAHATO: \n         SHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR SAHU: \n         SHRI SANJAY SADASHIVRAO MANDLIK: \n         SHRI MANOJ TIWARI: \n         SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE: \n         SHRI SUDHEER GUPTA: \n          \n         Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the number of unmanned railway crossings in the country, State-wise; \n(b) the number of unmanned railway crossings that are proposed to be \nconverted into manned crossings over the next five years, State-wise;  \n(c) whether the Government is considering the cons truction of underpasses \nand overbridges at various railway crossings in the country especially \nDelhi/NCR, Odisha, Jharkhand, Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra to ease \nvehicular traffic congestion;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the time by which these co nstructions are \nlikely to be completed; and \n(e) the steps taken/being taken by the Government to complete these \nconstructions in a time bound manner? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n\n(a) & (b): There is no unmanned level crossing (UMLC) on Broad Gauge (BG) \nroutes on Indian Railway.   However, as on 01.04.2020, total 948  \n \nUMLCs on Meter Gauge(MG) and Narrow Gauge (NG) are existing, which are \nplanned for elimination alongw ith Gauge Conversion works in future.  \nStatewise list of UMLC on Meter Gauge/ Narrow Gauge (MG/NG) is appended. \n(c) & (d): As on  01.04.2020, Railways have sanctioned 1 566 Road Over \nBridges (ROBs) and 6219 underpasses/ Road Under Bridges (RUBs)  i n the \ncountry including Delhi/NCR, Odisha, Jharkhand, Madhya Pradesh and \nMaharashtra.   Government is actively considering the construction of \nunderpasses and overbridges at various Level Crossings (LCs). However, the \nconstruction of ROB/RUBs depends upon the consent of State Government \nfor closure of LCs & cost sharing, wherever applicable,  availability of \nencroachment free land for approach roads, technical feasibility, shifting of \nutilities,  allocation of adequate funds by State agencies, public suppor t etc.  \nTherefore, it is not feasible to fix timelines for completion of these \nROB/RUBs. \n(e): Railways has taken pro -active measures in close coordination with \nvarious stakeholders to improve the progress of construction of \nROBs/RUBs/Subways as under: \n Joint survey with State Government to finalize the alignment & General \nArrangement Drawing (GAD). \n Standardization of design & drawings for various spans.  \n Regular coordination meeting with State Government officials. \n Construction of ROB on single entity basis. \n Monitoring of progress at different levels. \n***** \n\nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (b) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 294 BY SHRI MAHESH SAHOO, SHRI BIDYUT BARAN MAHATO, \nSHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR SAHU, SHRI SANJAY SADASHIVRAO MANDLIK, SHRI \nMANOJ TIWARI , SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE AND  SHRI SUDHEER GUPTA  \nTO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 03.02.2021 REGARDING UNMANNED \nLEVEL CROSSINGS. \nSTATEWISE UNMANNED LEVELCROSSINGS AS ON 01.04.2020 \nSN STATES MG NG Total \n1 Andhra \nPradesh 0 0 0 \n2 Assam 0 0 0 \n3 Bihar 0 0 0 \n4 Chandigarh 0 0 0 \n5 Chattisgarh 0 0 0 \n6 Delhi 0 0 0 \n7 Goa 0 0 0 \n8 Gujarat 160 169 329 \n9 Haryana 0 0 0 \n10 Himachal \nPradesh 0 4 4 \n11 Jammu & \nKashmir 0 0 0 \n12 Jharkhand 0 0 0 \n13 Karnataka 0 0 0 \n14 Kerala 0 0 0 \n15 Madhya \nPradesh 0 137 137 \n16 Maharashtra 0 109 109 \n\n17 Manipur 0 0 0 \n18 Mizoram 0 0 0 \n19 Nagaland 0 0 0 \n20 Odisha 0 0 0 \n21 Puducherry 0 0 0 \n22 Punjab 0 0 0 \n23 Rajasthan 97 52 149 \n24 Tamilnadu 0 0 0 \n25 Telangana 0 0 0 \n26 Tripura 0 0 0 \n27 Uttar \nPradesh 51 2 53 \n28 Uttarakhand 0 0 0 \n29 West Bengal 0 167 167 \n Total 308 640 948 \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |295", "t": "Ongoing Projects in Hilly Regions", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 295 \n  ANSWERED ON 16.03.2021 \n  \nIMPLEMENTATION OF DDU-GKY \n \n*295.  SHRI GIRISH BHALCHANDRA BAPAT: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of steps taken by non-governmental  partner organizations to train the rural \nyouth and rural women in Maharashtra under the Deen Dayal Upadhyay Grameen \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY) ; \n(b)  the steps taken to achieve the training and jo b placement targets to be met by March \n2022; and \n(c)  the details of resources and funding directed to the Maharashtra State Rural Livelihood \nMission to achieve the targets set for March 2022?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a)to (c):  A Statement is laid on the table of the  House. \n \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 295 \ndue for answer on 16.03.2021 \n(a)   Under Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana  (DDU-GKY), Project \nImplementing Agencies (PIAs) including non-governme ntal partner organisations are mandated to \nset up the training centers as per the provisions m ade in Guidelines, Standard Operating Procedure of \nthe Scheme and the projects sanctioned by the State.  \n \nProject Implementing Agencies (PIAs) mobilise the e ligible rural poor youth from different \ntarget districts and enroll them for training in th e trade of their interest. After completion of the \ntraining, these PIAs support the youth in successful placement and provide post placement support to \nthe candidates within or outside the State. There i s a provision of providing placement to minimum \n70% of the trained candidates. The DDU-GKY Guidelin es provides for a mandatory coverage of \n33% women candidates. \n \n130 training centers established by 115 PIAs are pr oviding training to the candidates in the \nState of Maharashtra. The number of candidates trai ned and placed during Action Plan period 2019-\n22 (extended up to 2019-23) is 14,250 and 9,284 respectively. \n \n(b) For proper implementation of the scheme and to ensure that the projects are completed in \ntime, DDU-GKY follows a concurrent monitoring of pr ojects through State Rural Livelihoods \nMissions/ State Nodal Skills Mission in the State G overnment, and through the Central Technical \nSupport Agencies designated by Ministry. Further, Ministry holds periodic review meeting on Action \nPlans approved for the State of Maharashtra.  \n \nMaharashtra State Rural Livelihood Mission has orga nized Kaushal Melas, Community \nResource Person (CRP) workshops at village level in  which PIAs have participated to brief about \ntheir courses and placements available with them. M SRLM has also organized direct placement \ncamps with the help of PIAs to get placements to th e trained candidates. MSRLM has focused on the \ndemand driven courses as per the skill gap analysis survey.  \n \nState of Maharashtra under DDUGKY for Action Plan 2 019-22 was sanctioned a target of \n1,25,814 during the Empowered Committee meeting of NRLM held on 26 \nth  February, 2019. Due to \npandemic, the trainings have remained suspended during major part of the year 2020-21. Considering \nthis, Government of India has extended the Action P lan period (2019-22) by one year, i.e. up to 31 st  \nMarch 2023 for providing adequate time to States for completion of their targets.  \n \n(c) DDU-GKY is a demand driven schemes and funds ar e allocated to States as per demands \nagainst approved Action Plans. Central funds releas ed by the Government to the State of \nMaharashtra, corresponding State share and expendit ure by the State during current Action Plan \nperiod (2019-23) is as under: \n (in Rs.crore) \nFY Central Share released \nto the State Government \nof Maharashtra under \nDDU-GKY  \nState Share \nunder DDU-\nGKY  \nState share released Expenditure by \nState of \nMaharashtra \n2019-20 219.25 146.16 49.04 84.46 \n2020-21  \n(till \n28.02.2021) \n0.00 0.00 34.08 15.46 \nTotal 219.25 146.16 83.12 99.92 \n \nThe State of Maharashtra has adequate funds for implementation of the programme. \n \n********* \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |296", "t": "Visakhapatnam Chennai Industrial Corridor", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT FOR PROMOTION OF INDUSTRY AND INTERNAL TRADE \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 296. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 3RD FEBRUARY, 2021. \n \nVISAKHAPATNAM CHENNAI INDUSTRIAL CORRIDOR \n \n296. SHRI RAM MOHAN NAIDU KINJARAPU: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state:  \n                                                      वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्री \n(a)  the steps taken by the Government to speed up the development of \nVisakhapatnam Chennai Industrial Corridor;  \n \n(b)  the total funds allocated and released for the development of Visakhapatnam \nChennai Industrial Corridor;  \n \n(c)  whether any timeframe has been fixed for completion of the development project \nto avoid any delay and if so, the details thereof;   \n(d)  whether the State Government of Andhra Pradesh has submitted a proposal in \nOctober, 2018 for consideration of National Industrial Corridor Development and \nImplementation Trust; and  \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Union Government in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्योग म त्रालय‍में‍राज्‍ यम त्रर‍(श्रर सोम‍प्रकाश)‍‍ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI SOM PARKASH) \n \n(a)to(c):  Visakhapatnam Chennai Industrial Corridor (VCIC) is under implementation as \nPhase 1 of East Coast Economic Corridor (ECEC). Two nodes namely \nChittoor and Visakhapatnam are identified under VCIC. Consultant for master \nplanning and preliminary engineering for Chittoor Node has been appointed by \nNational Industrial Corridor Devel opment Corporation Ltd. (NICDCL). Further, \nfor Visakhapatnam node, the master planning and preliminary engineering is \ninitiated by the State Government. As the project is in initial stage of \ndevelopment, no funds are allocated/released and no timeframe could be fixed \nat this stage.  \n \n(d)&(e): The State Government of Andhra Pradesh had submitted a proposal for \ninclusion of two nodes namely Chittoor and Visakhapatnam as part of VCIC \nunder the National Industrial Corridor Development and Implementation Trust \n(NICDIT) mandate.  NICDIT in its meeting held on 30 th August, 2019 has \naccorded its approval for development of Vishakhapatnam and Chittoor as \npriority nodes in Phase-1 of VCIC.   \n                                                                   \n******** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |297", "t": "Coaching Terminal at Latur", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA  \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 297 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \n \nCOACHING TERMINAL AT LATUR \n \n297.   SHRI SUDHAKAR TUKARAM SHRANGARE: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the work for development of coaching terminal at Latur \nStation is under consideration;  \n \n(b)  if so, the reasons for delay in approval of the work; and \n \n(c) the time by which construction work on the project is likely to be \ntaken up? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) Yes, Sir. \n \n(b) & (c) Works have been prioritised for approval and execution on \nIndian Railways based on operational and commercial requirement. \nNeeds are being assessed to work out timelines for construction work. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |298", "t": "Import of Auto Components", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 298  TO BE ANSWERED ON 03 rd FEBRUARY, 2021 TO BE ANSWERED ON 03 rd FEBRUARY, 2021 \nIMPORT OF AUTO COMPONENTS 298. SHRI GAUTAM GAMBHIR: Will the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (वा�ण�य एवं उ�योग मं�ी ) be pleased to state: (a) whether the auto industry imports INR 1 Lakh Crore worth of components and if so, the (a) whether the auto industry imports INR 1 Lakh Crore worth of components and if so, the details thereof; (b) whether the Government is working on any plan to decrease imports by auto sector in furtherance of boosting local economy and becoming self sufficient; and (c) if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER okf.kT; ,oa m|ksx ea=ky; esa jkT; ea=h ¼Jh gjnhi flag iqjh ½ THE MIN ISTER OF STA TE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY (SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI ) (SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI ) \n(a) The value of imports of auto components in India for the last two years (2018 -2019 and 2019-20) and the current year (April –November vis -à-vis last year) are as under: Imports of Auto Components by India                                                                                          (In Rs. Lakh Crore) 2018-192019-202019-20 (Apr -Nov) 2020-21 (Apr -Nov) 1.23 1.09 0.74 0.55 Source: Department of Commerce, Government of India (b & c) : Automobiles and Auto components have been included in the Production -Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme approved by Government for 13 key sectors for enhancing India’s manufacturing capabilities. ***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |299", "t": "Nuclear Energy Production", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.299 \n TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nNUCLEAR ENERGY PRODUCTION \n \n299. SHRI B. Y. RAGHAVENDRA: \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTERbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is true that nuclear energy is going to be the main source of energy for Indi’s \nrising energy requirements in the near future; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the details of the present status of nuclear energy production in India; \n \n(d) whether the Government has any proposal to increase the capacity of nuclear energy \nproduction in the country; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES & PENSIONS AND \nPRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (DR.JITENDRA SINGH):     \n \n(a)&(b)Nuclear energy is a clean, environment friendly base load source of power available \n24X7. It also has huge potential which can ensure long term energy security of the \ncountry in a sustainable manner. Therefore nuclear energy is an important \ncomponent of the country’s energy mix and is being pursued along with other \nsources of energy in an optimal manner. \n \n(c) There are presently 22 reactors with a total capacity of 6780 MW in operat ion and \none reactor, KAPP-3 (700 MW) has been connected to the grid on January 10, 2021. \nIn addition, there are 8 reactors (including 500 MW PFBR being implemented by \nBHAVINI) totaling to 6000 MW under construction at various stages. \n \n(d) Yes, Sir.  \n \n(e) The Government has accorded administrative approval and financial sanction for \nconstruction of 12 nuclear power reactors - 10 indigenous 700 MW Pressurized \nHeavy Water Reactors (PHWRs) to be set up in fleet mode & 2 units of Light Water \nReactors (LWRs) to be set up in cooperation with Russian Federation. On \nprogressive completion of the projects under construction and accorded sanction, the \nnuclear capacity is expected to reach 22480 MW by 2031. The Government has also \naccorded ‘In-Principle’ approval for five new sites for locating nuclear power plants in \nfuture. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |3", "t": "Funds for Agricultural and Allied Start-up", "head": "O.I.H.\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n3\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n \n2\nND \n \nFEBRUARY, 2021\n \n \ne\n-\nMANDI IN MADHYA PRADESH\n \n \n†*3. \n  \nDR. KRISHNA PAL SINGH YADAV: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE\n  \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has started any scheme to introduce e\n-\nmandi in Madhya \nPradesh; \n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif\n \nso, the details thereof, location\n-\nwise; and \n \n(c) \n \nthe number of farmers being benefited by these mandis?\n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI NARENDRA  SINGH TOMAR)\n \n \n \n(a) to (\nc\n):\n \nA statement is laid\n \non the Table of the House.\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (\nc\n) OF L\nOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n  \n3\n   \nDUE FOR REPLY ON \n2\nND\n \nFEBRUARY, 2021\n.\n \n \n(a) to (c):\n \nGovernment of India has launched National Agriculture Market (e\n-\nNAM) \nScheme on 14th April, 2016. e\n-\nNAM is a \nvirtual platform integrating physical wholesale \nmandis/ markets of different States/ Union \nTerritories (UTs)\n \nto \nfacilitate\n \nonline trading of \na\ngriculture and horticulture commodities through transparent price disc\novery\n \nmethod to \nenable f\narmers \nto realize better remunerative prices for their produce\n.\n \nSo far, 80 mandis of Madhya Pradesh have been integrated with e\n-\nNAM platform. The \ndetails of mandis from Madhya Pradesh integrated with e\n-\nNAM platform are at \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n.\n \n \n \nAlready 10.64 Lakh\n \nfarmers have\n \ntransacted and availed \nbenefit \nof\n \ne\n-\nNAM\n \nin Madhya \nPradesh.\n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE\n-\nI\n \n \n \nMadhya Pradesh : Details of mandis integrated with e\n-\nNAM\n \n \nSr. No.\n \nState\n \nDistrict \n \nLocation of e\n-\nNAM mandis/ markets\n \n \n1\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nBarwani\n \nAnjad\n \n2\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nSatna\n \nNagod\n \n3\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nRaisen\n \nRaisen\n \n4\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nSehore\n \nNasrullaganj\n \n5\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nRaisen\n \nUdaipura\n \n6\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nHoshangabad\n \nBanapura\n \n7\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nKhargone\n \nBadwaha\n \n8\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nKhargone\n \nSanawad\n \n9\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nKhargone\n \nBhikangaon\n \n10\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nKhargone\n \nKarhi\n \n11\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nShivpuri\n \nShivpuri\n \n12\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nDhar\n \nGandhwani\n \n13\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nDhar\n \nKukshi\n \n14\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nNarsinghpur\n \nKareli\n \n15\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nChhindwara\n \nSaunsar\n \n16\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \