������� ������ � ��������������������������\n��� ���������� ��� ������������� �\n�������������\n���������������������\n��������������������������\n��� ����������� � �����������������\n��� ���� � ����� �������� ������\n������������������������\n��������\n��� ������ ����� � �����������������\n������������������������ ��������\n��� ��������� ������������ � ��������\n���� ��������� ��������� � �����������������\n�\n��������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |358", "t": "National Mineral Exploration Trust", "head": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 358 \nANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nNATIONAL MINERAL EXPLORATION TRUST \n358. SHRI RITESH PANDEY \nWill the Minister of MINES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government established a PPP model 'National Mineral  \nExploration Trust' (NMET) to encourage private sector participation and  for giving a \nfillip to mineral exploration in the country; \n(b) the number of private exploration agencies empanelled for the  NMET till date; \nand \n(c) the number of projects approved for NMET along with the  details of the Mineral -\nwise  and  State- wise  distributions  of  mineral exploration  projects  approved \nunder the aforesaid project till date? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF MINES, COAL AND PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n \n(a) The Government has established  National Minerals Exploration Trust (NMET) for \ngiving a fillip to mineral exploration in the country. It has not been established on a \nPPP model. \n \n(b) No private exploration agencies have empanelled for the NMET till date. \n \n(c) A total of 191 number of projects have been approved till date by NMET. Details \nof the mineral and state wise approved projects are given below; \ni. Mineral-wise distribution of mineral exploration projects approved till date; \nSl. No. Commodity No. of Projects \n1 Iron Ore 18 \n2 Limestone 77 \n3 Manganese 18 \n4 Bauxite 16 \n5 Copper 7 \n6 Gold 6 \n7 Gold and Basemetal 4 \n8 Basemetal 7 \n9 Copper and Gold 2 \n10 Fe-Ni-Cr 1 \n11 Tin 1 \n\n12 Coal/Lignite 4 \n13 PGE 1 \n14 Diamond 2 \n15 Andalusite 1 \n16 Fertilizer Minerals 4 \n17 Tungsten 1 \n18 Magnesite 1 \n19 Environmental Studies 1 \n20 Associated Minerals 5 \n21 Molybdenum 1 \n22 Baseline Geoscience Surveys 13 \n  Total 191 \n  \n(ii)  State-wise distribution of mineral exploration projects approved till date; \nS. No. Name of the State No. of Projects \n1 Andhra Pradesh 12 \n2 Chhattisgarh 18 \n3 Jharkhand 9 \n4 Karnataka 11 \n5 Kerala 2 \n6 Madhya Pradesh 12 \n7 Maharashtra 7 \n8 Nagaland 2 \n9 Odisha 32 \n10 Rajasthan 19 \n11 Tamil Nadu 9 \n12 Telangana 44 \n13 Uttar Pradesh 1 \n14 Baseline Geoscience Survey 13 \n  Total 191 \n  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |359", "t": "Central Investment", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PLANNING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 359 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nCENTRAL INVESTMENT \n \n†359. SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT: \n       \n      Will the Minister of PLANNING be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the quantum of central investments made in the country, especially in the backward and \nrural areas as on date during the last three years, year-wise; \n \n(b) the names of the States where the quantum of investments made is lesser than other \nStates; and \n \n(c) the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING \nAND MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c): The information is being collected. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |36", "t": "Paddy Crop", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n36\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 2\nND\n \nFEBRUARY, 2021\n \n \nPADDY CROP\n \n \n36. \n \nSHRI G.S. BASAVARAJ: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE   \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state: \n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether it is a fact that paddy farmers from Punjab have sold out record bumper crop \nof paddy at MSP of Rs. 1,988/\n-\n \nper quintal for the 2020\n-\n21 season; and \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ \u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n   \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n \n(a) & (b)\n:\n \n \nThe Minimum Support Price (MSP) of paddy fixed by Government of India for \nKharif Marketing Season 2020\n-\n21 is Rs. 1868/qtl for Paddy Common and Rs. 1888/qtl. for \nPaddy Grade ‘A’ variety. During \nKharif Marketing Season 2020\n-\n21, a record quantity of \n202.77 LMT paddy has been procured in Punjab at MSP fixed by Government of India \nbenefitting 14.89 lakh farmers and Rs. 38,284 Crore paid towards MSP to the farmers of \nPunjab.\n \n \n*******\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |360", "t": "Aarogya Setu App", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 360 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nAAROGYA SETU APP \n \n360.     SHRI NATARAJAN P.R.: \n \nWill the Minister of ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   be \npleased to State: \n \n(a) whether the Aarogya Setu App was created under the PPP mode; \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the terms and conditions of private developers \nrole in the development of the app; and \n(c) the details of the action plan proposed by the Government to leverage the second \napp in view of less number of users of this contract tracing app? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR   ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION  TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI SANJAY   DHOTRE) \n \n(a):  Yes, Sir. T he Aarogya  Setu App has been developed by National Informatics \nCentre, in partnership with individual volunteers from industry and academia. \n \n(b):    The Individual volunteers from industry and academia made their contributions \nto the App development on a pro-bono basis in an individual capacity. \n \n(c):    Aarogya Setu is the single contact tracing App of Government of India with \nmore than 16 Crore registered Users. This makes Aarogya Setu the largest App based \ncontact tracing platform in the world. \n \n******** \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |361", "t": "Support on Farm Bill", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.361\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021\nSUPPORT ON FARM BILL\n361.    SHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL:\n  SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI:\n           \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether some countries including PIOs have given support to the\nagitation  of  Indian  farmers  against  three  bills  passed  by  Indian\nParliament;\n(b) if so, the names of the countries where such protest took place and\nstatements issued by some country heads in support of farmers\nagitation;\n(c) whether  the  Government  has  taken  up  the  matter  with  these\ncountries warning them not to interfere in the internal matters of\nIndia; and\n(d)  if so, the details of  the view point of those countries?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS [SHRI V\nMURALEEDHARAN]\n(a) & (b)  No  foreign  government  has  given  support  to  agitation  of\nIndian farmers against three bills passed by Indian Parliament. In Canada,\nUK, USA, and in few European countries, protests by a few motivated PIO’s\non issues related to the Indian Farm Bill have been reported. Canadian PM\nJustin Trudeau made a comment on issues related to farmers in India. \n(c) & (d)  We have taken up this matter with the Canadian authorities\nboth  in  Ottawa  and  New  Delhi  and  conveyed  that  such  comments\npertaining  to  the  internal  affairs  of  the  India  are  unwarranted,\nunacceptable  and  would  damage  India-Canada  bilateral  relations.\nGovernment  of  Canada  has  welcomed  the  Government  of  India’s\ncommitment to ongoing dialogue with the farmers to discuss issues of\nconcern. \n***"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |362", "t": "Natural Rubber Farmers", "head": "                     \n \n \n           GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                                    MINISTRY OF CULTURE \n                                     LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 362 \n  TO BE ANSWERED ON 22.03.2021 \n \n \nRENOVATION OF HISTORICAL BUILDINGS \n \n*362. SHRI UPENDRA SINGH RAWAT: \nSHRI RAMESH BIDHURI: \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state:- \n  \n (a) whether any survey of historically important buildings including   \nmonuments/forts has been conducted and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-\nwise, particularly in Uttar Pradesh, Delhi and Bhagalpur district of Bihar; \n(b) whether most of these buildings/forts/monuments are in  dilapidated condition \nand are in urgent need of repairs and further maintenance;  \n (c) if so, the details of such building/forts/monuments in the country, State/UT-wise  \nand the list of buildings repaired in Uttar Pradesh, Delhi and Bihar during the \nlast three years, year-wise, district-wise and location-wise along with the funds \nallocated and spent thereon; \n (d) whether the Archaeological Survey of India proposes to take over these \nforts/buildings/heritage sites and ensure proper  upkeep and maintenance \nthereof; and \n (e) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken for the proper maintenance \nof ancient monuments, particularly in Delhi? \n \n \n       ANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR CULTURE & TOURISM \n \n              (SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n \n \n \n(a)to(e) A statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION 