70\nANSWERED ON 04.02.2021\nAIBP IN UTTAR PRADESH\n†470. SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether any proposal sent by the Government of Uttar Pradesh under Accelerated Irrigation Benefit\nprogramme (AIBP) is pending for approval;\n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and\n(c) the time by which these proposals are likely to be sanctioned?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI & SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA)\n(a) to (c) During 2016 -17, ninety-nine (99) on -going Major/Medium irrigation projects (and their 7\nphases) under PMKSY -AIBP having ultimate irrigation potential of 76.03 lakh hectare and balance\nestimated cost of Rs.77,595 crore [Central Assistance (CA) component of Rs.31,342 crore] have been\nprioritized in consultation with States for completion in phases. Funding mechanism through\nNABARD has also been approved by the Government for both Central and State share of all prioritized\nprojects. CA is released from time to time as and when eligible CA proposals have been received from\nthe State Government(s).\nOut of the above prioritized projects taken up under PMKSY -AIBP, four (4) projects,\nnamely Bansagar Canal, Arjun Sahayak, SaryuNaharPariyojana (National Project) and Madhya Ganga\nCanal Ph-II are from Uttar Pradesh. Total CA and State Share of Rs 1,006.07 crore and Rs.4,111.61\ncrore respectively, has been released to these projects during 2016 -17 to 2019 -20. During 2020-21, so\nfar CA and State S hare of Rs.391.84 crore and Rs.1,270.40 crore respectively, has been released for\nthese projects of UP under PMKSY -AIBP. Presently, no proposal for the release CA and State Share\nfor these projects is pending with this Ministry.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |471", "t": "Solar Power Water Pumps", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-471 \nANSWERED ON-04.02.2021 \n \nSOLAR POWER WATER PUMPS \n \n+471.  SHRI PRADEEP KUMAR SINGH \n         SHRI BALAK NATH \n         SHRI RANJEETSINGH HINDURAO NAIK NIMBALKAR  \n         SHRI SUNIL KUMAR SINGH  \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has launched or proposes to launch any scheme to provide subsidy \nfor setting up of solar power water pumps;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set up solar water pumps from the Member of \nParliament Local Area Development Fund on the lines of Atal Jyoti Yojna; and  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (I/C) FOR NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY, POWER and MoS \nfor  SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) & (b)  The Ministry of New and Renewable Energy is implementing Pradhan Mantri Kisan \nUrja Suraksha evam Utthaan Mahabhiyaan (PM-KUSUM Scheme), which, inter alia, provides \nfor: \n \n(i) installation of 20 lakh standalone off-grid solar water pumps for irrigation purpose; and \n(ii) solarization of 15 lakh existing grid-connected agriculture pumps. \n \nUnder the Scheme, for installation of standalone solar pumps or solarization of existing \nagricultural pumps, central financial assistance of 30% of the cost of the benchmark cost or the \ncost discovered through tender, whichever is lower, will be provided. The State Government will \nalso provide subsidy 30% or higher. For North Eastern states including Sikkim; states of \nHimachal Pradesh and Uttarakhand; UTs of Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh; and island UTs of \nLakshadweep and A&N Islands higher CFA of 50% of the benchmark cost or the tendered cost, \nwhichever is lower, will be provided. Installation of standalone sola r pumps and solarization of \nexisting agricultural pumps can be done for pump of capacity higher than 7.5 HP. However, in \nsuch cases central financial assistance will be limited to that applicable for pump capacity of 7.5 \nHP.    \n(c) & (d) There is no proposal to set up solar water pumps from the Member of Parliament Local Area \nDevelopment (MPLAD) Fund. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |472", "t": "Use of Public Land in Central Vista Redevelopment Project", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 472 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 04, 2021 \n \nUSE OF PUBLIC LAND IN CENTRAL VISTA REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT \n \nNO. 472.  SHRI SANTOKH SINGH CHAUDHARY: \nSHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \nADV. DEAN KURIAKOSE: \nSHRI K. MURALEEDHARAN: \nSHRI ANTO ANTONY \nSHRI T.N. PRATHAPAN: \nDR. AMAR SINGH: \nSHRI UTTAM KUMAR REDDY NALAMADA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the total area of land for public use that has been  notified for  \nrestricted Government use to implement the Central Vista \nRedevelopment Project; \n(b)  whether the Government has received representations  from \nurban planners, heritage experts and the general pu blic \nexpressing objections to the project; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof including  the reasons for objections; \n(d)  The steps taken by the Government to address those \nobjections; \n(e)  whether the Government withdrew Delhi’s candidature  as a \nUNESCO World Heritage Site in 2015 in anticipation of the \nproject; and \n(f)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a)  to (d) The total area of land for public use that h as been notified \nto restricted Government use to implement the Central Vista Project is  \n \nContd on...2/ \n\n \n-2- \n \nNIL. The Central Government offices are permitted u se in  Public and \nSemi-Public Facilities (PSP) land use zones, vide N otification \nS.O.3348(E) dated 17.10.2017. In view of the said n otification, the land \nuse of four plots from Public/ Semi-Public (Socio C ultural) to \nGovernment Office use have been carried out.  These  plots are mostly \nbeing used at present for Government Office purpose only.  \nThere were 1,292 representations received by DDA which broadly \nincluded objections with regard to grant of Environ mental Clearance, \nChange of Land Use, conservation of heritage, curre nt economic \nscenario and COVID-19 health emergency. All represe ntations and \nsuggestions were duly considered. \n(e) & (f) There is no link between withdrawal of De lhi’s candidature as \na UNESCO World Heritage Site with Central Vista Pro ject as the \nwithdrawal was done in the year 2015 and the Centra l Vista Project \nhas been conceived in 2019.  \n \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |473", "t": "Public Objections regarding Central Vista Redevelopment Project", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 473 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBUARY 04, 2021 \n \nPUBLIC OBJECTIIONS REGARDING CENTRAL VISTA \nREDEVELOPMENT PROJECT \n  \nNO. 473.  ADV. DEAN KURIAKOSE: \n                   SHRI MOHAMMED FAIZAL P.P.: \n                   SHRI BALUBHAU ALIAS SURESH NARAYA DHANORKAR: \n                   DR. AMAR SINGH:   \n   \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be p leased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  the reasons for which the Delhi Development Au thority (DDA) \nprovided only two days’ time to hear the public’s o bjections to \nand suggestions on the changes in land use pattern in relation \nto the Central Vista Redevelopment Project? \n(b)   whether a review of the process of hearing th e public \nobjections to the changes in land use patterns will  be \nundertaken; and \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the rea sons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI)  \n \n(a) to (c)   Delhi Development Authority (DDA) has informed that  the \npublic notice inviting objections/suggestions for change in land use \nwas issued on 21.12.2019 giving 30 days time.  In response, 1,292 \nobjections/suggestions were received.   The Board of Enquiry and  \n \nContd. 2/-  \n \n\n-2- \n \n \n \nHearing, set up by the DDA to hear the objections/suggestions from \npublic conducted its proceedings on 6 \nth  and 7 th  February, 2020.  The \nentire process has been conducted under the provisions of section \n11-A of the Delhi Development Act, 1957 and there is no proposal to \nreview it.    \n  \n  \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |474", "t": "Allocation under Pre and Post Matric Scholarship Schemes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 474 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2021 \n \nALLOCATION UNDER PRE AND POST MATRIC SCHOLARSHIP SCHEMES \n \n474. SHRIMATI PRAMILA BISOYI: \n \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of Union Budget allocations, utilisation and unspent balances available \nwith States under Pre and Post Matric Scholarships for the religious minority \nstudents for the years 2017-18, 2018-19, 2019-20, State-wise; \n(b) whether the Government is considering an upward revision of the unit cost of pre \nand post -matric scholarships to the religious minority students, if so, the details \nthereof and the time by which the Government would notice such an increase of the \nscholarship amount and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) the steps taken by the Union Government in recent years to address the \neconomic poverty of the religious minority in the country; and \n(d) the total number of beneficiaries under skill improvement training programmes \nconducted for religious minorities during last three years, State-wise? \n  \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS  \n(SHRI MUKHTAR ABBAS NAQVI) \n \n(a): The details of budget allocated and amount utilized under Pre-Matric and Post \nMatric Scholarship Schemes for the religious minority students for the years 2017 -\n18, 2018-19, 2019-20 are as under: \n(In Rs Crore) \n \nS. \nNo. \n \nScheme \n2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 \nBudget \nallocated \nAmount \nutilized \nBudget \nallocated \nAmount \nutilized \nBudget \nallocated \nAmount \nutilized \n1. Pre- \nMatric \n1108.13 1108.13 1269.00 1176.19 1324.84 1324.84 \n2. Post \nMatric \n561.29 479.72 500.00 354.89 482.66 428.77 \n \nThe scholarships are disbursed directly to beneficiaries through DBT under these \nSchemes and neither any State -wise allocation of fund is made nor any amount is \nreleased to them against disbursement of scholarships. \n\n \n(b): The aforesaid  Scholarship Schemes for Minorities are proposed for \ncontinuation beyond 2020-21. As such, all aspects, including raising the number and \namount of scholarships or otherwise are to be looked into by this Ministry during the \nprocess of approval of these schemes for such period. \n \n(c): The Government has implemented the following welfare schemes to address \nthe economic p overty for the six (6) centrally notified minority communities namely, \nBuddhist, Christian, Jain, Muslim, Parsi and Sikh ,especially economically weaker & \ndowntrodden sections, across the country:-  \n \n(1) Pre -Matric Scholarship Scheme, Post -Matric Scholarship Schem e, Merit -cum-\nMeans based Scholarship Scheme - For educational empowerment of students. \n(2) Maulana Azad National Fellowship Scheme - Provide fellowships in the form of \nfinancial assistance. \n (3) Naya Savera - Free Coaching and Allied Scheme - The Scheme aims to provide \nfree   coaching to students/candidates belonging to  minority communities for \nqualifying in entrance examinations of technical/ professional courses and \nCompetitive examinations.   \n(4) Padho Pardesh - Scheme of interest subsidy to students of minority communities \non    educational loans for overseas higher studies.  \n(5) Nai  Udaan - Support for students clearing Prelims conducted by Union Public \nService Commission (UPSC), State Public Service Commission (PSC) Staff \nSelection Commission (SSC) etc. \n (6) Nai  Roshni - Leadership development of women bel onging to minority \ncommunities. \n (7) Seekho Aur Kamao - Skill development scheme for youth of 14 - 35 years age \ngroup and aiming at improving the employability of existing workers, school dropouts \netc. \n (8) Pradhan Mantri Jan Vikas  Karyakram (PMJVK) restructured in May 2018 earlier \nknown as MsDP – Implemented for the benefit of the people from all sections of the \nsociety  in identified Minority Concentration Areas for creation of assets in education, \nskill and health sectors.  \n(9) Jiyo Parsi - Scheme for containing population decline of Parsis in India. \n(10) USTTAD (Upgrading the Skills and Training in Traditional Arts/Crafts for \nDevelopment) launched in May 2015. \n(11) Nai Manzil - A scheme for formal school ed ucation & skilling of school dropouts \nlaunched in  Aug. 2015.  \n(12) Hamari Dharohar- A scheme to preserve rich heritage of minority communities \nof India under the overall concept of Indian culture implemented since 2014-15. \n (13) Maulana Azad Education Foun dation (MAEF) implements education and skill \nrelated schemes as follows: - (a) Begum Hazrat Mahal National Scholarship for \nMeritorious Girls belonging to the Minorities (b) Gharib Nawaz Employment Scheme \nstarted in 2017-18. for providing short term job orie nted skill development courses to \n\nyouth belonging to minority communities. (c) Bridge Course for madarsa students & \nschool dropouts by Aligarh Muslim University, Aligarh and Jamia  Millia Islamia, New \nDelhi under Nai Manzil scheme. (d) Swachh Vidyalaya. \n (14) Equity to National Minorities Development and Finance Co"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |475", "t": "Collateral Free Loans to MSMEs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 475\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 04.02.2021\n \n \nCOLLATERAL FREE LOANS TO MSMEs\n                                                                                                                       \n \n475.              SHRI D.K. SURESH:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n    \nwhether, Mic\nro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) are given collateral free \nloans;\n \n(b)\n   \nif so, the total amount of loan sanctioned and disbursed for MSMEs during the last three \nyears State/Year\n-\nwise;\n \n(c)\n    \nwhether the Government has received any complaints from M\nSMEs about denial of \ncollateral free loans from banks; and\n \n(d)\n   \nif so, the details thereof?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) & (b):\n \nYes\n,\n \nSir.  The Credit Guarantee Trust for Micro and Small Enterprises  \n(\nCGTMSE) provides guarantees to various eligible Micro and Small units financed by the \nbanks and financial institutions to facilitate collateral free loans. The upper limit for such \nloans is Rs. 2 crore. As a part of Atmanirbhar Bharat package, Government a\nlso announced \nthe Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS) which is a Rs. 3 lakh crore \ncollateral\n-\nfree lending program with 100 percent credit guarantee for businesses including \nMSMEs. The State\n-\nwise/year\n-\nwise details of the loans under CGTMSE and St\nate\n-\nwise \ndetails of the credit under ECLGS are given at Annexure I and Annexure II respectively. \n \n \n(c) & (d):\n \n \nAll proposals that are eligible under the relevant guidelines for a collateral free \nloan are generally\n \naccepted. However, Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises \n(MSME)\n \nsometimes receives complaints regarding denial of collateral free loans by the \nBanks.  As there is a prescribed procedure for obtaining a collateral free loans, such \ncomplaints rece\nived in the Ministry of MSME, are accordingly forwarded to concerned Bank \nfor consideration as per the rule/procedure.   \n \n \n \n******\n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \nAnnexure \nreferred to in reply to part (a)&(b) of Lok Sabha Unstarred \n \nQuestion  No. 475 for answer on\n \n04.02.202\n1\n \nSr. \nNo.\n \n \n \nStates and Uts\n \nFY 18\n-\n19\n \nFY 19\n-\n20\n \nFY 20\n-\n21 (till 31.12.2020)\n \nNo.  of \nGuarantees\n \nApproved \nAmt (in \nRs. CR)\n \nNo. of \nGuarantees\n \nApproved \nAmt (in \nRs. CR)\n \nNo. of \nGuarantees\n \nApproved \nAmt (in \nRs. CR)\n \n1\n \nAndaman & Nicobar\n \n332\n \n30.10\n \n264\n \n29.45\n \n192\n \n15.55\n \n2\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n29812\n \n979.41\n \n50562\n \n1556.78\n \n27322\n \n744.64\n \n3\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n347\n \n24.28\n \n415\n \n46.95\n \n360\n \n37.53\n \n4\n \nAssam\n \n12978\n \n792.69\n \n14070\n \n686.72\n \n9422\n \n490.16\n \n5\n \nBihar\n \n18464\n \n1295.92\n \n24531\n \n1303.32\n \n16848\n \n762.30\n \n6\n \nChandigarh\n \n7752\n \n335.31\n \n1778\n \n133.61\n \n987\n \n67.36\n \n7\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n5252\n \n497.30\n \n14022\n \n705.70\n \n8872\n \n377.96\n \n8\n \nDadra & Nagar \nHaveli\n \n111\n \n24.69\n \n256\n \n26.88\n \n233\n \n18.35\n \n9\n \nDaman & Diu\n \n73\n \n27.14\n \n191\n \n32.48\n \n274\n \n12.52\n \n10\n \nDelhi\n \n13615\n \n1350.09\n \n24917\n \n2182.94\n \n9475\n \n1041.73\n \n11\n \nGoa\n \n1353\n \n120.22\n \n2594\n \n183.07\n \n1628\n \n101.63\n \n12\n \nGujarat\n \n21423\n \n2104.14\n \n58595\n \n3859.49\n \n30607\n \n2004.26\n \n13\n \nHaryana\n \n5179\n \n628.92\n \n25916\n \n1582.88\n \n14070\n \n806.60\n \n14\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n2682\n \n209.69\n \n7538\n \n436.78\n \n6021\n \n316.14\n \n15\n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n11724\n \n348.33\n \n12887\n \n416.03\n \n12611\n \n419.90\n \n16\n \nJharkhand\n \n11281\n \n1244.52\n \n15340\n \n1116.03\n \n10638\n \n595.