Road Development Programme in \nNorth East (SARDP-NE)”, State-wise and phase-wise; \n(b)  the details of projects identified under the scheme along with \nthe present status thereof; and \n(c)  whether the Government is planning to discontinue the said \nscheme if so, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n(a)   Rs 3,640 crore has been allocated for SARDP -NE works \n(including Arunachal Prade sh Package of SARDP -NE) in the North \nEastern states out of which an expenditure of Rs. 3314 crore has \nbeen incurred during financial year 2020 -21. SARDP-NE works in a \nlength of 285 km for Rs. 5020 crore have been sanctioned during \n2020-21. \n\n(b)   Government of India has given approval for 2/4 laning of 6418 \nkm of various categories of roads under Phase ‘A’ and Arunachal \nPradesh of SARDP-NE in North East at an estimated investment of \nabout Rs. 30,450 crore. Apart from the above Government of India \nhas also given approval for preparation of detailed project report \nfor 3723 km of roads under Phase ‘B’ of SARDP -NE. Details of \nprojects completed, ongoing and  yet to be awarded under SARDP -\nNE Phase -A and Arunachal Pradesh Package of SARDP -NE are \nplaced at Annexure -A, Annexure -B and Annexure -C respectively. \nDetails of projects identified under Phase-B of SARDP-NE is placed \nat Annexure-D. \n(c)   There is no such plan to discontinue the SARDP-NE scheme. \n  \n\nANNEXURE – A \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (b ) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 516 FOR ANSWER ON 04.02.2021 ASKED \nBY SHRI VINCENT H. PALA REGARDING SPECIAL ACCELERATED \nROAD DEVELOPMENT PROGRAMME IN NORTH EAST (SARDP-NE) \nList of Completed Projects \n \nSL. \nNo. \nName of Projects Length \n(in \nKm) \nSanctioned \nCost (Rs. in \ncr.) \n1 2 laning from Mahadevpur to Buri Dihing section of NH -\n52B        \n25.13 136.60 \n2 2 laning  from Bordumsa -Namchik (Buri Dihing-\nJairampur) road on NH52-B (New NH-215) from Km 0.15 \nkm (starting Chainage near Buridihing Bridge) to km \n22.380 \n22.23 189.91 \n3 2 laning from Pasighat to Pangin section of NH -229 from \nkm 0 to Km 28  \n26.58 299.66 \n4 2 laning from Pasighat  to Pangin section of NH -229 from \nkm 41.3 to 58.420 (Existing Km 42 to km 59)  \n17.12 247.44 \n5 Construction of 2 -lane road from existing km. 37.500 of \nHunli-Anini road (Near Ithun Bridge) to Km. 53.50 - Pkg.II \n16.00 259.52 \n6 2 laning of Singer river to Sijon nala   23.38 238.46 \n7 2 laning from Changlang Dist Boundary – Khonsa \n(42.844 km) section of NH-52B       \n42.84 438.32 \n8 2 laning with paved shoulders from Pasighat  to Bomjur \nsection from km 583.450 to 605.600 including \nRealignment from km591.900 to 602.600  \n22.15 244.82 \n9 Strengthening of NH -37 from Santipur –Meka (length - \n19.50 Km) \n19.50 38.04 \n10 Two laning of NH-153 from Km 24.00 to Km 40.00.  16.00 42.31 \n11 Two laning of NH-153 from Km 40.00 to Km 56.485. 16.49 48.94 \n12 Double Laning of Papu -Yupia-Hoj-Potin Road Km 0.000 -\n10.000 in Arunachal Pradesh Under SARDP -NE \n(Package-A)  \n9.96 92.84 \n13 Double Laning of Papu-Yupia-Hoj-Potin Road Km 10.000 \n- 32.000 in Arunachal Pradesh Under SARDP -NE \n(Package-B) \n20.04 201.19 \n\n14 Double Laning of Papu -Yupia-Hoj-Potin Road (NH -229)  \nKm 32.000 - 53.000 in A runachal Pradesh Under \nSARDP-NE(Package-C) \n \n19.06 165.11 \n15 Four Laning of Itanagar to Holongi  Section of NH -52A \n(Km 0.000 to 19.260)  \n19.26 475.22 \n16 Two laning of Pasighat – Pangin Road (NH -229) for the \nstretch of Km 28.00 to Km 41.30. (Package-II) \n12.75 165.23 \n17 Two laning of Road from Pasighat  –Singer from km 0.00 \nto 19.885 River. (Length-19.887 Km) \n19.89 138.84 \n18 Two laning of Road from Yingkiong –Gobuk.(0.00 Km to \n25.20 Km) \n25.20 233.98 \n19 Construction of Bridges across Dibang and Lohit river \nsystems including approach roads between Chowkham-\nDigaru and Bomjur -Meka in the state of Arunachal \nPradesh on DBFOT annuity basis \n29.63 1595.45 \n20 Two laning of Pasighat – Pangin Road (NH -229) for the \nstretch of Km 57.00 to Km 71.596 (Package-IV) \n14.60 137.50 \n21 Two laning of Road from Gobuk –Sijhon Nalla from Km \n26.210 to 75.485.(Length - 49.275 Km) \n49.28 389.45 \n22 Lumla - Tashigaon 47.85 103.77 \n23 Akajan - Likabali - Bame 8.62 33.39 \n24 Joram - Koloriang 20.00 148.81 \n25 Meka to Roing from Km 3.824 to Km 0(Link -I) and sector \nRoing to Hunli  from Km 0.00 to Km 16.00 (Link -II) total \nlength 19.224 Km \n19.22 155.47 \n26 Meka (Roing) to Koronu from km 632.450 to 650.615 18.16 198.79 \n27 Koronu-Paya stretch of NH -52 from km 650.615 to km \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |518", "t": "NHAI Projects in Rajasthan and Maharashtra", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 518 \nANSWERED ON 4TH FEBRUARY, 2021 \n  \nNHAI PROJECTS IN RAJASTHAN AND MAHARASHTRA \n  \n518. SHRI RANJEETSINGH HINDURAO NAIK NIMBALKAR: \n SHRI SUDHAKAR TUKARAM SHRANGARE: \n SHRI BHAGIRATH CHOUDHARY: \n  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग  मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the length in kilometers of new highway project approved by \n National Highway Authority of India (NHAI) since the year  2014 \nincluding the number of projects completed and under  construction \nas on date in the country; \n  \n(b) whether new highways have been constructed in Rajasthan \n and Maharashtra as part of the said projects of NHAI and if  so, the \ndetails thereof, location and kilometer-wise along with  the funds \nallocated and utilised thereon so far; \n  \n(c) the time frame set for completion of the above mentioned \n approved and under construction projects; \n  \n(d) whether any proposal from Rajasthan and Maharashtra (MH)  is \npending with the Union Government regarding the road  projects \nincluding Madha Parliamentary Constituency (MH);  and \n  \n(e) if so, the time by which these proposals are likely to be \n approved?  \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANSWER \n  \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) Total 26717 km length of National Highways has been awarded by \nNational Highways Authority of India (NHAI) since 2014. Out of this, \nworks in a length of 16394 km have already been completed and balance \nworks in 10323 km are under implementation. \n(b) & (c) During this period, total 68 projects with aggregate length of \nabout 2615 km having sanctioned cost of Rs. 42073 crore have been \nenvisaged in the State of Maharashtra covering 26 National Highways. \nOut of 68 projects, 08 projects with aggregate length of 491 km having \ntotal cost of Rs. 6890 crore have been completed and work for remaining \n60 projects is under impl ementation. All these projects  targeted for \ncompletion by  March, 2023. The overall expenditure incurred on these \nprojects is about Rs. 22908 crore. \nTotal 65 projects with aggregate length of about 4417 km having \nsanctioned cost of Rs. 41112 crore have been envisaged in the State of \nRajasthan covering 22 National Highways. Out of 65 projects, 18 projects \nwith aggregate length of 2029 km having total cost of Rs. 7229 crore \nhave been completed and work for remaining 47 projects is under \nimplementation. All these projects targeted for completion by January, \n2023. The  overall expenditure incurred on these projects is about Rs. \n19685 crore. \n (d) & (e) National Highway projects have been taken up for construction \ndepending upon project preparation as well as readiness of the proposal \nin terms of pre -construction activit ies. As such no proposal is pending \nwith NHAI. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |519", "t": "Relief Subsidies to MSME Entrepreneurs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 519\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON: 04.02.2021\n \n \nRELIEF SUBSIDIES TO MSME ENTREPRENEURS\n \n \n519\n.\n       \n         \nSHRI SANJAY KAKA PATIL:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL & MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government proposes to give relief subsidies or fund to MSME \nentrepreneurs due to COVID pandemic \nsituation\n;\n \n(b)\n \nif so, the details thereof; and\n \n(c)\n \nwhether\n \nthe Government proposes to relax the taxation & bank loan schedule for \nMSMEs due to  Covid\n-\n19 pandemic situation and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a) & (b)\n:\n \nGovernment has implemented a judicious mix of fiscal and monetary policies \nalong with regulatory and structural reforms to mitigate the negative impact of COVID\n-\n19 on \nthe MSME entrepreneurs.  Government has already announced a series of measures  in this \nd\nirection, which inter\n-\nalia includes Rs. 3 lakh crore collateral\n-\nfree lending program with 100 \npercent credit guarantee for businesses including MSMEs, Rs. 20,000 crore subordinate debt \nfor stressed MSMEs with partial guarantee, Rs. 45,000 partial credit gu\narantee scheme 2.0 for \nnon\n-\nbanking financial companies (NBFCs), housing finance companies (HFCs) to do fresh \nlending to MSMEs, Rs. 50,000 crore equity infusion for MSMEs through Fund of Funds, \ncredit facility for street vendors (PM SVANidhi). \n \n \n(c)\n:\n \nOn the\n \ntaxation front, Government has taken some regulatory and compliance \nmeasures such as postponing tax\n-\nfiling and other compliance deadlines, reduction in penalty \ninterest rate for overdue GST filings. Government has introduced IBC related relaxations for \nMS\nMEs, amongst others.  Moreover, with a view to facilitate meaningful restructuring of \nstressed MSME accounts, RBI has permitted a one\n-\ntime restructuring of loans to MSMEs. \nThe restructuring of the MSME borrower account under the revised guidelines is to be\n \nimplemented by March 31, 2021 and such borrower accounts which may have slipped in to \nNPA category between March 2, 2020 and date of implementation may be upgraded as \n‘Standard asset’ as on the date of implementation of the restructuring plan. \n \n \n******\n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |52", "t": "Financial Assistance for Sugarcane Farmers", "head": "ORIGINAL IN HINDI\nGOVERNIUENT OF INDIA\nMINTSTRY OF GONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtc DtsTRtBUTtol{\nDEPARTMENT OF FOOD AND PUBLIG DISTRIBUTION\nFINANGIAL ASSISTANCE FOR SUGARCANE FARMERS\nt52. SHRI PARBATBHAT SAVABHA! pATEL:\nSHRI NARANBHAI KAGHHADIYA:\nWill the minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND pUBLtC\nDIETRIBUTION Jrrtffrr arrd, urc.a gk Trdufr6, fuflq d+ be pteased to state:\n(a) the amount of financial assistance sanctioned by the Govemment for\nsugarcane farmers in terms of crores of rupees during the month of December;\n(b) the framework prepared to transfer the said assistance direct to the\naccounts of the farmersi and\n(c) the numbef of sugarcane farmers likely to be benefited from the said\ndeclsion?\nANSWER\niitNtsTER oF STATE FOR MtNtSTRy OF CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & pUBLtC\nDISTRIBUTION\n(sHRt DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO)\n(a): With a view to facilitate export of sugar during the sugar season 2O2O-21\nand thereby improving the liquidity position of sugar mills enabling them to clear\ncane price dues of famers for sugat season 2O2O-21, Central Government has\napproved Rs. 35O0 crores for providing assistance to sugar mills for expenses on\nmarketing costs including handling, upgrading and other processing costs and\ncosts of intemational and anternal transport and freight charges on export of\nsugar.\n(b): ln order to ensure that the assistance is directly credited into the\naccounts of farmers, the sugar mill shall open a separate no-lien account in a\nnationalized bank/cooperative bank and furnish to that bank the list of farmers\nalong with bank accounts detalls and extent of cane price dues payable to the\nfarmers for the sugar season 2O2O-21 and cane price arrears of previous sugar\nseasons, duly certilied by the Cane Gommissioner / Director of Sugar of the state\nconcerned. The bank shall credit the amount of assistance to the famers'\naccounts on behalf of the mills against cane dues payable and subsequent\nbalance, if any, slrall be credited anto mallts account.\n(c): The decision wil! improve the liquidity position of sugar mills and enable\nthem to clear cane plice dues of farmers. There are about 5 crore sugarcane\nfarmers including thear famalies, whach wall be benefited by this dec:sion.\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO, 52\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 2\"a Februaryt 2021"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |521", "t": "Online Initiative of KVIC", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 521\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2021\n \n \nONLINE INITIATIVE OF KVIC\n \n \n521. \n \nSHRI POCHA BRAHMANANDA REDDY: \n \n \n \nSHRI N. REDDEPPA: \n \n \n \nDR. BEESETTI VENKATA SATYAVATHI:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate:\n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has launched the ekhadiindia.com as the first ever \neffort of the Ministry & Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC) in online \n& B2C outreach;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) \n \nthe targeted sales and revenue generation projection for the next financial year?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a)&(b):\n  \n  \nYes Sir, Khadi\n \nand Village Industries Commission (KVIC), a statutory \nbody, working under the aegis of the Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium \nEnterprises, Government of India, established a B2C official online \ne\n-\ncommerce \nportal namely ‘\nekhadiindia.com’ to support the on\nline marketing facilities for its \nstakeholders \non 1\nst\n \nJanuary, 2021. This portal has been established on Design, Build, \nFinance, Operate and Transfer (DBFOT) model through Public\n-\nPrivate Partnership \n(PPP) mode on revenue sharing basis. The contract is init\nially for a period of 10 years. \n \n \n(c):\n \n \nThere is no sales target fixed as on now for the next financial year.\n \n \n* * * * *\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |522", "t": "Bridge Connecting Mallawan and Bilhaur in Uttar Pradesh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 522 \nANSWERED ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2021   \n  \nBRIDGE CONNECTING MALLAWAN AND BILHAUR IN UTTAR PRADESH \n  \n522. SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT:  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government is aware that due to absence of bridge on \nGanga river people have to pass through nearby Unnao district to \nconnect Mallawan and Bilhaur region in Uttar P radesh resulting in \nwastage of time and money;  \n(b) if so, whether the Government has taken any steps or proposes to \ntake steps to construct a bridge on Ganga river to connect Mallawan \nand Bilhaur region; and  \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \n(a) No Sir. there is no NH   connecting Mallawan and Bilhaur, however \nthere exists a 2 lane bridge over river Ganga on State Highway 40 \n\nwhich connects Bilhaur to Bangarmau   on State Highway  38. \nBangarmau and Mallawan are connected through State Highway 38. \nThe total distance between Bilhaur to Mallawan  via this route is \nabout 37.5 km.  \n(b) and (c) As such central government has no plan to construct a new \nbridge on Ganga to connect Bilhaur and Mallawan region.  \n  \nxxxxx \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |523", "t": "Jal Shakti Abhiyan -II", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 523\nANSWERED ON 04.02.2021\nJAL SHAKTI ABHIYAN -II\n523. SHRI SUNIL DATTATRAY TATKARE DR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR S.\nDR. AMOL RAMSING KOLHE SHRI KULDEEP RAI SHARMA\nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE DR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has launched Jal Shakti Abhiyan-II recently;\n(b) if so, the details thereof and the aims and objectives behind the move along with the States to be\ncovered under the Abhiyan-II;\n(c) whether the Jal Shakti Abhiyan -I covering all states has achieved the desired results and if so, the\ndetails thereof; (\nd) whether the campaign has been able to bring together officers, groundwater experts and scientists from\nthe Union Government to work together with State and District officials in country‘s water stressed\ndistricts and if so, the positive outcome of such interaction; and\n(e) the other steps taken by the Government to make water conservation a Jan Andolan through asset\ncreation and extensive communication?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI & SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT\n(SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA)\n(a) No, Sir.\n(b) does not arise.\n(c) & (d) Department of Drinking Water and Sanitation, Ministry of Jal Shakti launched Jal Shakti\nAbhiyan (JSA)-I, in 1592 blocks out of 2836 blocks in 256 water stressed districts of the country in two\nphases last year (1 July to 30 September and from 1 October to 30 November 2019) as a time bound\ncampaign intended to improve water availability in these blo cks. Under Jal Shakti Abhiyan -I, officers,\ngroundwater experts and scientists from the Government of India have worked with State and District\nofficials in these water -stressed districts of the country to promote water conservation and water resource\nmanagement by focusing on accelerated implementatio n of five target interventions, viz, water\nconservation & rainwater harvesting, renovation of traditional and other water bodies/tanks, reuse and\nContd…P/2\n\n//2//\nrecharge of bore wells, water shed de velopment and intensive afforestation. With this campaign, huge\nawareness has been generated and various stakeholders, viz. government department, agencies, NGOs,\nofficials, Panchayats, individuals, etc. have started taking steps for water conservation.\n(e) Water being a State subject, steps for augmentation, conservation and efficient management of water\nresources are primarily undertaken by the respective State Governments. Central Government augments\nthe efforts of the State Governments by providing te chnical and financial assistance to them through\nvarious schemes and programs. Ministry of Jal Shakti has been implementing various schemes and\nprograms like Atal Bhujal Yojana (Atal Jal), National Aquifer Mapping and Management (NAQUIM)\nProgram, Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana - Accredited Irrigation Benefit Program (PMKSY-AIBP),\nCommand Area Development & Water Management (CADWM) Program, Surface Minor Irrigation and\nRepair Renovation & Restoration of water bodies (a part of PMKSY - Har Khet Ko Pani ) etc and\ncampaigns like “Catch the Rain” and “Sahi Fasal” with people’s/farmers’ active participation for water\nconservation and asset creation.\nThe \"Catch The Rain\" campaign launched by National Water Mission is an awareness\ngeneration program nudging t he state governments and stakeholders to take up rain water harvesting\nstructures appropriate to the soil-substrata and climatic conditions, with active participation of people. In\ncollaboration with the \"Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan\" a massive awareness drive has been launched on\n21 December 2020 involving Youth Clubs in 623 districts. Apart from this National Water Mission has\nbeen holding seminars, workshops, monthly \"Water Talks\" and \"Water Tech talks\" and weekly webinars\n\"Catch the Rain: Dialogues wi th DMs\" with selected District Magistrates/District Collectors/Deputy\nCommissioners to spread awareness.  Department of Rural Development is also taking up water\nconservation works in drought prone areas of the country in all States/UTs under Mahatma Gand hi\nNational Rural Employm ent Guarantee Scheme (MGNREGS) as per demand and following due process\nunder the scheme.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |524", "t": "Road Accidents", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 524  \nANSWERED ON 4TH FEBRUARY, 2021 \nROAD ACCIDENTS \n \n524. SHRIMATI APARAJITA SARANGI:  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n(a)  The number of reported cases of road accidents in state and \nnational highways during the last three years in the country, \nState/UT-wise;  \n(b)  Whether there has been an increase in such cases of reported cases \nin the country;  \n(c)  If so, the details thereof including the percentage increase of such \ncases reported from Odisha during the said period and the reasons \ntherefor;  \n(d)  Whether the Government has devised any mechanism to study and \nanalyse the cause of road accidents; and  \n(e) The steps taken by the Government to reduce the instances of  road \naccidents? \nANSWER \n \n  THE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n      (SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n \n(a)  & (b)   As per the data received from police department of all States/UTs \nthe total  number of  road accidents on National Highways including \nExpressways and State Highways  in the country during last three calendar \nyears and the current year i.e. 2017 to 2019 are shown in the table below  \n(Figures in bracket represents the percentage change over previous year) \n\n \n \n \n     The total number road accidents on Highways for the last three years are \nat Annexure-I. \n \n(c )   Total number of road accidents on National Highways including \nExpressways and State Highways in the State Odisha during the last three \ncalendar years i.e. 2017 to 2019 is given in the table below:- \n \nYears Total \nNumber of \nRoad \naccidents  \nin the State \nof  Odisha  \nTotal Number \nof Road \naccidents on \nNational \nHighways in \nOdisha \npercentage \nshare of Road \nAccident on \nNational \nHighway in the \nState of  \nOdisha to total \naccidents \nTotal \nNumber of \nRoad \naccidents \non State \nHighways \npercentage \nshare of Road \nAccident to \ntotal accidents \non State \nHighways in \nthe State of \nOdisha \n2017 10855 \n(3.07) \n4487 \n(6.08) 41.34 \n3445 \n(3.52) 31.74 \n2018 11262 \n(3.75) \n4207 \n(-6.66) 37.36 \n3104 \n(-9.90) 27.56 \n2019 11064 \n(-1.76) \n4148 \n(-1.42) 37.49 \n3195 \n(2.93) 28.88 \n \n(d) & (e)  The Ministry of Road Transport & Highways has notified “Member of \nParliaments’ Road Safety Committee” in each district of the country to \npromote awareness amongst road users under the chairmanship of Hon’ble \nMember of Parliament (Lok Sabha) from the district.  \n \nThe Ministry has formulated a multi -pronged strategy to address the \nissue of road safety based on Education, Engineering (both of roads and \nYear Total Number of \nRoad accidents \non all roads \nTotal Number \nof Road \naccidents on \nNational \nHighways \npercentage \nshare of Road \nAccident on \nNational \nHighway to \ntotal \naccidents \nTotal \nNumber of \nRoad \naccidents \non State \nHighways \npercentage \nshare of Road \nAccident on \nNational \nHighways to \ntotal \naccidents \n2017 4,64,910 \n(-3.3) \n1,41,466 \n(-0.6) 30.4 \n116158 \n(-4.52) 25 \n2018 4,67,044 \n(0.5) \n1,40,843 \n(-0.4) 30.2 \n117570 \n(1.22) 25.2 \n2019 4,49,002 \n(-3.8) \n1,37,191 \n(-206) 30.5 \n108976 \n(-7.31) 24.3 \n\nvehicles), Enforcement and Emergency Care. Accordingly, various initiatives \nhave been taken by the Ministry as detailed below:- \n(i) Education:   \n The Ministry implements a scheme for undertaking publicity measures \nand awareness campaigns on road safety to create awareness among \nroad users through the electronic media, print media, NGOs etc.  \n Observance of National Road Safety Week every year for spreading \nawareness and strengthening road safety. \n A Certification Course for Road Safety Auditors has been commenced \nin Indian Academy of Highway Engineers (IAHE). \n  \n(ii) Engineering (both of Roads and vehicles) \n Road engineering \n High priority to identification  and rectification of black spots \n(accident prone spots) on national highways. \n Road safety has been made an integral part of road design at \nplanning stage. \n The threshold for four laning of National Highways have been \nreduced from 15,000 Passenger Car Units (PCUs) to 10,000 PCUs. \n Ministry has delegated powers to Regional Officers of MORTH for \ntechnical approval to the detailed estimates for rectification of \nidentified Road Accident black spots. \n Guidelines for pede strian facilities on National Highways for \npersons with disabilities have also been issued to all States / \nUTs. \n \n Vehicle engineering: \n Safety standards for automobiles have been improved.  \n Ministry has notified fitment of Speed Limiting devices on all \ntransport vehicles  \n\n Scheme for setting up one model Inspection & Certification \nCentre in each State/UT with Central assistance for testing the \nfitness of vehicles through an automated system \n \n(iii) Enforcement  \n The recently passed motor vehicles (Amendment) Act, 2019 provides \nfor strict enforcement through use of technology and further \nprovides for strict"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |525", "t": "Road Safety", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 525  \nANSWERED ON 4TH FEBRUARY, 2021 \nROAD SAFETY \n525. MS. RAMYA HARIDAS:  \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n(a) whether faulty road design and complex coordination mechanism \nof Government agencies are the major hindrances in ensuring road \nsafety in the country;  \n(b)  if so, the reaction of the Government thereto;  \n(c)  whether the Government is taking any initiative to strengthen the \nprovisions relating to motor vehicles and make road contractors \nand consultants accountable for faulty road design and \nconstruction; and  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n  THE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n      (SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) &   (b)    No Sir.  Road Accidents occur due to multiple causes such as \nover speeding, drunken driving/consumption of alcohol, driving on wrong \nside/lane indiscipline, fault of the driver of motor vehicle,  use of mobile \nphones during driving , mechanical defect/fault of the vehicle defect in \nroad condition, weather condition and     lack of knowledge on road \nsignage etc. These various factors can broadly be categorized into human \nerror, road condition/environment and vehicular condition that  lead to \naccidents on roads. \n \n(c) & (d)  The Motor Vehicles (Amendment) Act, 2019, recently passed by \nthe Parliament has inserted a new Section 198A in the Motor vehicles Act, \n1988 which provides as under:- \n\n“198-A Failure to comply with standards for road design, construction and \nmaintenance- \n (1)      Any designated authority, contractor, consultant or concessionaire \nresponsible for the design or construction or maintenance of the safety \nstandards of the road shall follow such design, construction and \nmaintenance standards, as may be prescribed by the Central Government \nfrom time to time.  \n(2)      Where failure on the part of the designated authority, contractor, \nconsultant or concessionaire responsible under sub-section (1) to comply \nwith standards for road design, construction and maintenance,  results in \ndeath or disability, such authority or contractor or concessionaire shall \nbe punishable with a fine which may extend to one lakh rupees and the \nsame shall be paid to the Fund constituted under section 164B.” \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |526", "t": "Sports coaching centres", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 526 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04/02/2021 \n \nSports coaching centres \n \n†526. SHRI RODMAL NAGAR: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any plan to provide sports \nequipments in various sports coaching centres in the country and if \nso, the details thereof State-wise including Uttar Pradesh;  \n \n(b) whether the sports equipments available in  various sports training \ncentres are regularly checked; \n \n(c) if so, the details and the outcome thereof; and  \n(d) the other measures being taken by the Government to ensure the \nmaintenance of sports equipment and to keep them in working \ncondition? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) Sports is a State Subject and the primary responsibility of \ndevelopment of sports, including providing sports equipments in \nvarious coaching centres in the cou ntry, rests with the State \nGovernments and with the National Sports Federations (NSFs) , which \nare responsible for governance of individual sports disciplines. The \nCentral Government, through the sports development schemes \nimplemented by it and organizations functioning under its aegis, \ncomplements and supplements the efforts of the State Governments \nand NSFs in this regard.  \n\n \nSports Authority of India (SAI), an autonomous body under the \naegis of the Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports , provides sports \nequipment in all its training Centres across the country, including in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh, for training of players.  \nIn addition, the Khelo India – National Programme for \nDevelopment of Sports also provides for grant of financial support \ntowards equipment to academies accredited under the Support to \nNational/Regional/State Sports Academies vertical and to State Level \nKhelo India Centres under the State Level Khelo India Centre vertical  \nof the Scheme.  \n \n(b) & (c) The sports equipment in SAI centres are regularly checked by \nCoaches of concerned disciplines and corrective measures are taken \nas per requirement.  \n(d) The equipment in SAI are maintained regularly or replaced as per \nrequirement. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |527", "t": "Registration of MSMEs", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.527 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n04.02.\n2021\n \n \nREGISTRATION OF MSMEs\n \n \n527.\n \n      \nCOL. RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE:\n \n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be pleased to state: \n \n \n(\na\n)\n \nthe total number of MSMEs registered in the country, State\n-\nwise;\n \n(\nb\n)\n \nthe details of proposals made to increase the ease of registration of MSMEs on the \nudyamregistration\n.gov.in\n \npor\ntal;\n \n(\nc\n)\n \nthe number of rural enterprises registered as MSMEs in the Country, State\n-\nwise ;\n \n(\nd\n)\n \nthe details of any campaigns or initiatives undertaken to increase awareness of \nMSMEs and their registrations on a national or State level; \n \n(\ne\n)\n \nthe details of any policies \nconsidered along with the national logistics policy, to \nincrease ease of doing business with MSMEs;\n \n(\nf\n)\n \nthe steps taken in this direction and measures to streamline  and make easy the \nprocess of registration of MSMEs on the Government e\n-\nMarketplace platform?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI NITIN GADKARI)\n \n \n(a): \n \n \nThe details are at annexure\n-\nI and II.\n \n \n(b):\n \n \nTo increase the ease of registration on \nUdyam Registration portal, the Ministry of \nMSME has made the registration process hass\nle free by making it paperless, online and \nwithout any supporting documents and fee. The portal has linkages with Income Tax, GST \nportals for fetching the investment and turnover figures automatically. \n \n \n(c):  \n \nThe annexure\n-\nI and II include rural enterpris\nes also.\n \n \n(d): \n \nThe Ministry of MSME, vide notification no. S.O.2119(E) dated 26.06.2020, has \ncreated t\nhe Champions Control Rooms functioning in various institutions and offices of the \nMinistry of \nMSME \nincluding the Development Institutes (MSME\n-\nDI)\n \nthat \nsh\nall act as \nSingle Window Systems for facilitating the registration process and further handholding the \nMSMEs \n \nin all possible manner.\n \nThe District Industries Centres (DICs)\n \nunder State \nGovernments/UT administrations \n \nalso\n \nact as Single Window facilitation Systems in their \nDistricts.\n \nThe Government is also running campaigns in social media to popularize the \nUdyam Registration and to spread awareness about the same.\n \n \n \n \n\n \n: 2 :\n \n \n \n(\ne\n):\n \nOnline filing of Udyam\n \nRegistration and Champions\n \nPortal for speedy online\n \nredressal of grievances are the steps taken by Ministry of MSME to increase Ease of Doing \nBusiness. The Udyam registration Portal has facility to link the registrant with the GeM \nplatform to participate \nin Government’s mandatory procurement program. In addition, the \nportal has a provision to link MSMEs to the TReDs portal for factoring of bills. \n \n \n(\nf\n):\n \nMinistry of MSME is making every attempt to encourage the MSMEs to get \nthemselves onboarded on the GeM portal\n. As on 02.02.2021, 506186 MSEs (sellers and \nservice providers) are registered on the GeM portal and around 57.84% (orders value \nMSE% ) has been placed with MSEs through GeM.  All the field offices attached with this \nMinistry have also been requested to en\ncourage more number of MSEs for onboarding \nthemselves on the GeM Portal for supply of goods or services.\n \n \n \n********\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI referre\nd to in reply to part (a) \n \nof the Lok Sabha \nUnstarred \nQuestion No. 5\n27\n \nfor \nanswer on 04.02.2021\n \n \nTotal MSME Registered Till 30/06/2020 Under Udyog Aadhaar Memorandum (UAM)\n \nSl. \nNo.\n \nState\n \nTotal \nMSME \nRegistered\n \nMicro\n \nSmall\n \nMedium\n \n1\n \nANDHRA PRADESH\n \n379903\n \n321640\n \n56572\n \n1691\n \n2\n \nARUNACHAL PRADESH\n \n1993\n \n1154\n \n756\n \n83\n \n3\n \nASSAM\n \n27618\n \n21900\n \n5336\n \n382\n \n4\n \nBIHAR\n \n938485\n \n904106\n \n33140\n \n1239\n \n5\n \nCHHATTISGARH\n \n78203\n \n64958\n \n12618\n \n627\n \n6\n \nGOA\n \n10285\n \n7188\n \n2913\n \n184\n \n7\n \nGUJARAT\n \n867502\n \n729338\n \n132104\n \n6060\n \n8\n \nHARYANA\n \n216115\n \n169417\n \n44535\n \n2163\n \n9\n \nHIMACHAL PRADESH\n \n16962\n \n11952\n \n4648\n \n362\n \n10\n \nJAMMU AND KASHMIR\n \n169595\n \n151740\n \n17339\n \n516\n \n11\n \nJHARKHAND\n \n411191\n \n333298\n \n74160\n \n3733\n \n12\n \nKARNATAKA\n \n143072\n \n119748\n \n22220\n \n1104\n \n13\n \nKERALA\n \n966975\n \n910808\n \n54400\n \n1767\n \n14\n \nMADHYA PRADESH\n \n1978529\n \n1739392\n \n229190\n \n9947\n \n15\n \nMAHARASHTRA\n \n37200\n \n31878\n \n5254\n \n68\n \n16\n \nMANIPUR\n \n2418\n \n2120\n \n281\n \n17\n \n17\n \nMEGHALAYA\n \n3547\n \n2597\n \n915\n \n35\n \n18\n \nMIZORAM\n \n2019\n \n1516\n \n479\n \n24\n \n19\n \nNAGALAND\n \n137947\n \n116399\n \n20748\n \n800\n \n20\n \nODISHA\n \n233277\n \n196265\n \n35896\n \n1116\n \n21\n \nPUNJAB\n \n623556\n \n547367\n \n73776\n \n2413\n \n22\n \nRAJASTHAN\n \n1081\n \n701\n \n342\n \n38\n \n23\n \nSIKKIM\n \n1106587\n \n969057\n \n133174\n \n4356\n \n24\n \nTAMIL NADU\n \n323346\n \n239420\n \n81562\n \n2364\n \n25\n \nTELANGANA\n \n6651\n \n5613\n \n1008\n \n30\n \n26\n \nTRIPURA\n \n970718\n \n885029\n \n82207\n \n3482\n \n27\n \nUTTAR PRADESH\n \n47869\n \n39661\n \n7639\n \n569\n \n28\n \nUTTARAKHAND\n \n269671\n \n234610\n \n33237\n \n1824\n \n29\n \nWEST BEN"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |528", "t": "Drinking Water", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION  \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 528  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2021  \n  \nDrinking Water \n528. SHRIMATI MEENAKASHI LEKHI: \nSHRI GOPAL JEE THAKUR: \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is contemplating initiation of new schemes with respect to water;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) the details of progress of Jal Jivan Mission, State/UT wise; and  \n \n(d) the details of number of households having clean drinking water facility? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI RATTAN LAL KATARIA) \n \n(a) & (b) To enable every rural household in the co untry to have assured potable water at service \nlevel of 55 litre per capita per day (lpcd) through  Functional Household Tap Connection (FHTC) \nby 2024, Government of India, in partnership with State Governments, is implementing Jal Jeevan \nMission (JJM) with an estimated outlay of Rs. 3.60 lakh Crore. At the time of announcement of \nthe JJM, only 3.23 Crore (17%) out of total 18.93 C rore rural households, had tap water \nconnections.   \n(c) & (d) As reported by States/ UTs, since announc ement, 3.32 Crore rural households have been \nprovided with tap water connections across the coun try and thus presently 6.55 Crore rural \nhouseholds (34.20%) have tap water supply. State/ U T-wise details of total number of households \nand households with tap water connections is in pub lic domain and available on the JJM \ndashboard @ \nhttps://ejalshakti.gov.in/jjmreport/JJMIndia.aspx . \n**** \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |53", "t": "Diversion of MGNREGS Funds", "head": "\u0001\u0002\u0003\u0004\u0005\u0006\u0007\u0004\u0006\b\t\u0002\n\t\u000b\u0006\f\u000b\r\t\n\u0007\u000b\u0006\u000b\u000e\b\u0005\u000f\t\u0002\n\t\u0005\u0010\u0005\r\u0011\t\f\u0004\u0003\u0004\u0011\u0002\u0012\u0007\u0004\u0006\b\t\n\f\u0004\u0012\r\u0005\b\u0007\u0004\u0006\b\t\u0002\n\t\u0005\u0010\u0005\r\u0011\t\f\u0004\u0003\u0004\u0011\u0002\u0012\u0007\u0004\u0006\b\t\n�����������\n��������������������������\n\t\t\r\u0006\u000e\u0013\u0004\u0005\u0004\f\t\u0002\u0006\t\u0014\u0015\u0016\u0014\u0015\u0016\u0015\u0014\u0015\u0017\t\n\t\n\f\u000b\u0003\u0004\u0005\u000e\u000b\u0002\u0006\t\u0002\n\t\u0007\u0001\u0006\u0005\u0004\u0001\u000e\t\n\u0010\u0006\f\u000e\t\n\t\n\u0018\u0019\u0016\t\t \u000e\u001a\u0005\u000b\t\u001b\r\u0006\u0010\u0007\u0010\u0005\u0010\t\u0005\r\u0001\u001a\u0010\t\u0005\r\u0007\r\u001b\u0005\u000b\u000e\u001a\u0006\r\t\u0005\r\u001c\u0010\u001d\t\n\t\n\u0013\u001e\u001f\u001f\t !\"\t\u0007\u001e#\u001e$ \"%\t&'\t\u0005\u0010\u0005\r\u0011\t\f\u0004\u0003\u0004\u0011\u0002\u0012\u0007\u0004\u0006\b\t(\"\t)\u001f\"*$\"+\t &\t$ * \"\u001d\t\n\t\n,*-\t\t .!\" !\"%\t !\"\t\u0001&/\"%#0\"# \t\u001e$\t*.*%\"\t !* \t1\"% *\u001e#\t\u000e  * \"\t\u0001&/\"%#0\"# $\t*%\"\t*1 \u001e#2\t*2*\u001e#$ \t \n !\"\t \u001e0)\u001f\"0\"# * \u001e&#\t &'\t \u0007*!* 0*\t \u0001*#+!\u001e\t \u0006* \u001e&#*\u001f\t \u00053%*\u001f\t \u00040)\u001f&40\"# \t \u00013*%*# \"\"\t\n\u000e1!\"0\"\t,\u0007\u0001\u0006\u0005\u0004\u0001\u000e-\t*#+\t+\u001e/\"% \u001e#2\t !\"\t'3#+$\t%\"\u001f\"*$\"+\t3 #+\"%\t !\"\t$1!\"0\"\t &\t& !\"%\t \n$1!\"0\"$\t*#+\t'&%\t& !\"%\t)3%)&$\"$5\t\n,(-\t\t \u001e'\t$&6\t !\"\t+\" *\u001e\u001f$\t !\"%\"&'5\t*#+\t\n,1-\t\t  !\"\t1&%%\"1 \u001e/\"\t0\"*$3%\"$\t(\"\u001e#2\t *7\"#\t(4\t !\"\t\u0001&/ \"%#0\"# \t &\t\u001e0)\u001f\"0\"# \t !\"\t$1!\"0\"\t \n)%&)\"%\u001f4\t*#+\t13%(\t !\"\t+\u0