0010\u0005\u0004-\t *#+\t \"$ *(\u001f\u001e$!0\"# \t &'\t \n\u001e#+\")\"#+\"# \t $&1\u001e*\u001f\t *3+\u001e \t 3#\u001e $\t *#+\t *))&\u001e# 0\"# \t &'\t \u00020(3+$)\"%$&#$\t \u001e#\t  !\"\t \u000e * \"$;\u0010\b$\u0016\t \u000e * \"\t \n$)\"1\u001e'\u001e1\t%\"/\u001e\".$\t*%\"\t*\u001f$&\t3#+\"% *7\"#\t'%&0\t \u001e0\"\t &\t \u001e0\"\u0016\t\n�\n�������� \n�\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |530", "t": "Implementation of AMRUT Scheme", "head": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 530 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 04, 2021 \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF AMRUT SCHEME \n \nNO. 530  SHRI DHAIRYASHEEL SAMBHAJIRAO MANE: \n SHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL: \n DR. SUJAY RADHAKRISHNA VIKHE PATIL: \n DR. HEENA GAVIT: \n SHRI HEMANT SRIRAM PATIL: \n DR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be p leased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  the steps taken for implementation of Atal Mis sion for \nRejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) schem e in \nMaharashtra till date; \n(b)  the details of the cities of Maharashtra selec ted for AMRUT \nscheme; \n(c)  the details of Detailed Project Report (DPR) a nd fund \nallocation for implementation of AMRUT scheme in \nMaharashtra; and \n(d)  the progress of AMRUT scheme and the time fram e for \ncompletion of projects under AMRUT scheme in Maharashtra? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a). Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transf ormation \n(AMRUT), was launched on 25 June 2015 in 500 select ed cities of \nthe country including 44 cities of the State of Maharashtra.  The  \nContd…2/ \n\n \n \n \n-2- \n \n \n \nMission period has been extended up to 31 March 2021. Government \nof India has already approved State Annual Action P lans (SAAPs)of \nState of Maharashtra amounting to ₹7,759.32 crore f or the entire \nMission, which include committed Central Assistance  of ₹3,534.08 \ncrore. As on date, Central Assistance amounting to ₹2,776.25 crore \nhas been released to the Government of Maharashtra for \nimplementation of projects under the Mission. \n \n(b). List of 44 cities of Maharashtra covered under  AMRUT has \nbeen attached as ANNEXURE. \n \n(c) & (d). As on date, State of Maharashtra has tak en up 196 \nprojects under AMRUT costing ₹7,825.66 crore, of wh ich, 133 \nprojects costing ₹787.83 crore have been completed,  63 projects \ncosting ₹7,037.83 crore are under implementation. S tate of \nMaharashtra has taken up projects in excess of thei r approved \nSAAP size and the entire excess cost shall be borne  by the State \nGovernment. \n \n \n**** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF PART (b) OF THE LO K \nSABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 530 FOR ANSWER ON 04 \nFEBRUARY, 2021: \n \n \nName of Cities of the State of Maharashtra selected under AMRUT \n \nAchalpur  Bhusawal  Jalna  Nashik  Solapur  \nAhmadnagar  Beed  Kalyan \nDombivali  \nNavi \nMumbai  Thane  \nAkola  Chandrapur  Kolhapur  Osmanabad  Udgir  \nAmbarnath  Dhule  Latur  Panvel  Ulhasnagar  \nAmravati  Gondiya  Malegaon  Parbhani  Vasai-Virar \nCity  \nAurangabad  Greater \nMumbai  \nMira \nBhayandar \n \nPimpri \nChinchwad  Wardha  \nBadlapur  Hinganghat  Nagpur  Pune  Yavatmal  \nBarshi  Ichalkaranji  Nanded \nWaghala  \nSangli-Miraj \nKupwad  Shirdi \nBhiwandi  Jalgaon  Nandurbar  Satara  -------- \n \n \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |531", "t": "National Young Leaders Programme", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF YOUTH AFFAIRS) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 531 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2021 \n \nNational Young Leaders Programme   \n \n531.  SHRIMATI GEETA KORA: \nSHRI JUGAL KISHORE SHARMA: \nSHRI DILESHWAR KAMAIT: \nSHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \na) the number of programmes organised in Madhya  Pradesh, \nJharkhand, Jammu & Kashmir and Bihar under  National Young \nLeaders Programme during the last  five years and the current year, \nState-wise; \nb) the funds released to these States during the last  five years \nalong with the achievements of Nehru Yuva  Kendras of Madhya \nPradesh, West Singhbhum district  of Jharkhand, Jammu district of \nJ&K and Supaul district of Bihar during the last five years?  \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR \nYOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n(a) The State wise details of number of programmes organized during \nthe last five years  under National Young Leaders Programme (NYLP) \nscheme (Neighbourhood Youth Parliament ) through Nehru Yuva \nKendra Sangathan ( NYKS) is at Annexure -I. Neighbourhood Youth \nParliaments could not be  organized during the year 2020 -21 due to \nCorona pandemic situation. \n \n(b) The details of the funds released  during the last  five years  to the \nstates of Madhya Pradesh, Jharkhand, J&K and Bihar  to NYKS under \nNYLP scheme  is at A nnexure-II. The achievements of Nehru Yuva \nKendras  in the state of  Madhya Pradesh, West Singhbhum district of \nJharkhand, Jammu district of J&K and Supaul district of Bihar  during \nlast five years is at Annexure-III.  \n*****\n\n \nANNEXURE-I  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART ( A) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED Q.NO. 531 FOR 04.02.2021 ASKED BY \nSHRIMATI GEETA KORA, SHRI JUGAL KISHORE SHARMA, SHRI DILESHWAR KAMAIT AND SHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA  \nREGARDING NATIONAL YOUNG LEADERS PROGRAMME. \n \nNumber of Neighbourhood Youth Parliaments organized under National Young Leaders Program in the State \nof Madhya Pradesh, Jharkhand, Jammu & Kashmir and Bihar during 2015-16 to 2019-20. \n 2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 2019-20 \nState No. of \nProgrammes \nNo of \nParticipants \nNo. of \nProgrammes \nNo of \