 CHARGE) OF THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a): The State/ Union Territory (UT)-wise details o f houses sanctioned, \nconstructed/ allotted under the Pradhan Mantri Awas  Yojana-Urban \n(PMAY(U) are at Annexure-I. \n \nContd…/2 \n\n-2- \n(b): Bank/ Primary Lending Institution (PLI) - wise  details of the loan \namount sanctioned and disbursed under Credit Linked  Subsidy \nSchemevertical of PMAY-U are at Annexure-II. \n (c): Yes, Sir. Against an assessed demand of aroun d 112 lakh houses \nunder the scheme, a total of 1,09,82,808 houses hav e been sanctioned; out \nof this, 41,78,578 have been constructed/delivered and remaining are at \nvarious stages of construction. Houses provided und er PMAY-U have \namenities like water supply, electricity, kitchen a nd toilet along with basic \nsocial and physical infrastructure. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-I referred in reply to LSUQ No 580 due for 04-02-2021  \nState UTs wise details of Houses Sanctioned and constructed under \nPMAY-U \n \n \nS. No \n \nStates/UTs No. of Houses \nSanctioned \nNo. of Houses \nConstructed \n1 A&N Island 612  40  \n2 Andhra Pradesh 20,26,446  3,57,151  \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 7,422  3,247  \n4 Assam 1,23,268  24,690  \n5 Bihar 3,60,703  78,157  \n6 Chandigarh 1,316  6,276  \n7 Chhattisgarh 2,62,615  1,24,123  \n8 UT of DNH & DD 7,170  4,608  \n9 Delhi (UT) 22,841  46,821  \n10 Goa 3,558  3,499  \n11 Gujarat 7,55,895  5,09,681  \n12 Haryana 2,78,832  34,686  \n13 Himachal Pradesh 12,209  4,944  \n14 Jammu & Kashmir 55,761  9,486  \n15 Jharkhand 2,12,822  92,291  \n16 Karnataka 6,72,304  2,16,882  \n17 Kerala 1,24,913  88,501  \n18 Ladakh (UT) 1,777  384  \n19 Lakshadweep (UT) - - \n20 Madhya Pradesh 8,40,999  3,95,793  \n21 Maharashtra 12,85,427  4,10,150  \n22 Manipur 50,176  4,925  \n23 Meghalaya 4,766  1,091  \n24 Mizoram 35,779  4,270  \n25 Nagaland 32,003  4,293  \n26 Odisha 1,73,476  83,258  \n27 Puduche