RRED QUESTION NO.972 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 8.2.2021 \n \n \nFUNDS RELEASED FOR SAFETY AND FACILITIES IN MONUMENTS \n \n+972. SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH JOSHI:  \nSHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \nSHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA:  \n \n \n Will the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is concerned for safety and convenience of the \ntourists visiting the protected monuments after Corona pandemic; \n(b) whether the Government has sanctioned/released any funds during the \nlast one year for providing facilities to the tourists visiting the said \nmonuments; and  \n(c) if so, the monument-wise details thereof? \n \n  \n \nANSWER \n \n        THE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR CULTURE AND TOURISM \n \n(PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n \n \n(a) Yes, Sir. The centrally protected monuments/sites have been opened for visitors \nsubject to following the preventing measures and Standard Operating Procedures \n(SOP) issued from time to time by Ministry of Home Affairs, Ministry of Health and \nFamily Welfare, Ministry of Culture and State/District administration. \n \n(b)&(c) The expenditure on providing visitors facilities at centrally protected \nmonuments/sites including ticketed monuments is met out from the overall \nsanctioned budget for conservation/preservation of monuments/sites.  The \nexpenditure incurred on conservation, preservation and annual maintenance of all \nmonuments during the last three years and provision for current year is at \nAnnexure.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b)&(c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 972 FOR 8.2.2021 \n \nDETAILS OF EXPENDITURE INCURRED FOR CONSERVATION, PRESERVATION AND ENVIRONMENTAL DEVELOPMENT  OF \nPROTECTED MONUMENTS DURING THE LAST THREE YEARS AND ALLOCATION FOR CURRENT FINANCIAL YEAR \n \n                                                                                                                   (Amount Rs. in Lakhs) \nSl. No. Name of