hine Smelting Alloy Pvt Ltd 29AABCE1590R1Z1 \n9 Rajmahal International Pvt Ltd 29AAECR7476A1Z7 \n10 Maan Trading 29AAICM3354L1Z0 \n11 Saroha Builders 29AAHCG2400L1ZM \n12 Adhi Batteries India Private Limited 29AALCA1785E1ZH \n13 Zikshoo Infratech Pvt Ltd 29AABCZ3458P1ZH \n14 Ambika Ispat Pvt.Ltd 29AACCA9396C1ZF \n15 Everett Infra & Equipments (P) Ltd. 21AADCE5929Q1ZA \n16 Parchalit Infra and Informedia Pvt. Ltd. 21AAACT0900D1ZC \n17 DB Merchandise Private Limited 33AAECD8372K1ZE \n18 Medley Merchandise Private Limited 33AAJCM2303E2Z1 \n19 Anmol Ferro Impex Pvt. Ltd. 33AAICA0948A1Z8 \n20 Nadesh Impex Pvt. Ltd. 33AAFCN3545B1ZX \n21 Vivan Trade Impex Pvt. Ltd. 33AAFCV6608K1Z4 \n22 Royal Meridian Impex India Private Limited 33AAGCR8330M2Z3 \n23 Chatwada Trading P Ltd 33AAHCC0817F1Z5 \n24 Vikmani Trading P Ltd 33AAFCV7363P1ZO \n25 Amodha Trade Links Pvt. Ltd. 33AAQCA3344J1ZL \n26 Iral Impex  07AAFCI1723E1ZZ \n27 Pusa Polymers Pvt. Ltd. 07AAACP6985C1ZB \n28 Busy Bee Overseas Pvt. Ltd. 07AAHCB5965F1ZI \n29 Sand Steel 36AAUCS0847G1ZY \n30 Filtus Infrastructure Limited 36AACCJ3140M1ZK \n\n \n \nPage 4 of 12 \n \n31 Parchalit Infra and Infomedia Private Limited 36AAACT0900D1Z1 \n32 Zenith Impex Pvt. Ltd. 08AAACZ2247D1Z1 \n33 Fedders Lloyd Pvt. Ltd. 08AAACF0437B1ZA \n34 Punj Technology Pvt. Ltd. 08AADCP8698P1Z9 \n35 Redical Engineering Solutions Pvt. Ltd. 08AAHCR1696P1ZJ \nS.No Name of the entity GSTIN \n36 Air Serco Pvt. Ltd. 08AAACA0023C1ZN \n37 Abide Electronics Pvt. Ltd. 08AANCA2075K1ZD \n38 PSL Engineering Pvt. Ltd. 08AAACP5284G1ZB \n39 Deny Marketing Pvt. Ltd. 08AAGCD6104K1ZN \n40 Swissline Intertrade Pvt. Ltd. 08AAJCS6595A1Z3 \n41 Mohit Metals Pvt Ltd 08AAECM0087C1ZR \n42 Windroot Infrabuild Pvt. Ltd. 08AABCU9079K1ZN \n43 Parchalit Infra and Infomedia Private Limited 08AAACT0900D1Z0 \n44 Navkar Builders Limited 08AAACN7211P1Z7 \n45 Radha Swami Infracon & Engineering 08AADCR2235E1ZP \n46 Real System Interiors Private Limited 08AAECR9231R2ZM \n47 Sarel Drill & Engineering Equipment India Pvt. Ltd 08AAXCS1185N1ZE \n48 Ghrishneswar Engineers (P) Ltd 19AACEG9732E2ZF \n49 Reeja Vyapaar (P) Ltd 19AAICR5448N1ZL \n50 Goldwright Vyapaar (P) Ltd 19AAHCG0428Q1ZG \n51 Sashmol and Nath Engineering Pvt. Ltd. 19AAUCS8534J1ZF \n52 Fazi Trading Pvt. Ltd 19AADCF3786E1ZG \n53 Sonartari Vinimay Pvt. Ltd 19AAZCS2670J1ZH \n54 Swarnabarsa Vinimay Pvt. Ltd 19AAZCS2603R1ZC \n55 Aatikah Sales Private Limited 19AAPCA1366H1ZF \n56 Daania Trading Private Limited 19AAKCM8571F1ZZ \n57 Hitakrit Trading Private Limited 19AAECH0802Q1ZD \n58 Virikia Marketing Pv"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |996", "t": "Piped Natural Gas Connections", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 996 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 8th February, 2021 \nPiped Natural Gas Connections \n \n996.  SHRIMATI NUSRAT JAHAN RUHI : \nSHRIMATI JASKAUR MEENA:  \nSHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE: \n \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम और \u0000ाकृ\u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ी \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government is supplying/proposes to Supply natural gas to all the states of the \ncountry through pipelines, if so, the State-wise details thereof including Maharashtra, West \nBengal and Rajasthan;  \n(b) whether the Government proposes to provide domestic and industrial piped gas in Ramtek \ndistrict of Maharashtra, various cities/districts of West Bengal, specially in the District of 24 \nParganas and Dausa in Rajasthan during the next two years;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor including the details of upcoming \nschemes/ future projects proposed to be implemented; and  \n(d) whether any programme is being run by the Government for the use of other green fuels in \nfuture, if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम और \u0000ाकृ\u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ी \n(\u0000ी धम\u0000\u0000\u0000 \u0000धान) \nMINISTER OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n  \n(a)  Petroleum & Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) is the authority to grant authorization \nto the entities for the development of City Gas Distribution (CGD) network in Geographical \nAreas (GAs) as per PNGRB Act, 2006.  So far PNGRB has authorized 232 GAs for development \nof CGD network across country up to 10th CGD Bidding Round covering more than 400 \ndistricts in the country in 27 States/Union Territories (UTs) including Maharashtra, West Bengal \nand Rajasthan.  \n \n\n(b) To provide Piped Natural Gas (PNG) to domestic and industrial customers are part of the \ndevelopment of CGD network. PNGRB has authorized Hindustan Petroleum Corporation \nLimited (HPCL) for development of CGD networks in North 24 Pargana and South 24 Pargana \ndistricts of West Bengal under 10 th CGD bidding round. Ramtek district of Maharashtra and \nDausa in Rajasthan have not yet been authorized for development of CGD network. \n \n(c) PNGRB identifies GAs for authorizing the development of CGD network in synchronization \nwith the development of natural gas pipeline connectivity, natural gas availability and techno-\ncommercial viability. \n \n(d) With respect to use of other green fuels in future, Government has launched a scheme of \nSustainable Alternative Towards Affordable Transportation (SATAT) on 1 st October 2018 to \npromote Compressed Bio-Gas (CBG) as an alternative and green transport fuel.  SATAT \ninitiative envisages establishing 5000 Biogas plants across the country by the year 2023-24 \nwhichmay generate approx. 15 Million Tonnes per annum of Biogas.  \nAlso, Government has notified the ‘National Policy on Biofuels-2018’ on 04 June, 2018. \nGovernment is adopting a multi-pronged approach to promote and encourage use of biofules by \nblending ethanol in petrol through Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) Programme using ethanol \nderived from multiple feedstock, development of Second Generation (2G) ethanol technologies \nand its commercialization for augmenting ethanol production and blending biodiesel in diesel \nthrough Biodiesel Blending Programme. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |997", "t": "IIIT", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION\nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 997\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.02.2021\nIIIT\n997. SHRI KOMATI REDDY VENKAT REDDY:\nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Indian Institute of Information Technology(IIIT) has called\nfor applications from students and graduates to develop their ideas into\nproducts, at its incubator and provides two options-entrepreneur in\nresidence(EiR) and a grants programme through EiR programme which\nis open to those who can develop and validate their ideas into a proof of\nconcept and will allow entrepreneurs to work from the ‘Gyan circle\nventure(GCV)‘ incubator; and\n(b) if so, the details thereof and progress made?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF EDUCATION\n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’)\n(a) & (b) : Gyan Circle Ventures (GCV) is the Technology Business Incubator\n(TBI) of Indian Institute of Information Technology (Public-Private Partnership)\n[IIIT(PPP)] Sri City (Chittoor). This TBI is funded under the Technology\nIncubation and Development of Entrepreneurs (TIDE) 2.0 Scheme of Ministry\nof Electronics & Information Technology for promoting innovation and\nentrepreneurship in Information Technology (IT) and its application areas.\nUnder the TIDE 2.0 Scheme, applications are invited from potential innovators\nand startups for “Entrepreneur in Residence” and “Startup Grants”. Although\nthe responses were poor due to COVID-19 pandemic, efforts have been put to\nreach out to local colleges in Andhra Pradesh and Tamil Nadu.\nApart from IIIT (PPP) Sri City (Chittoor), other IIITs viz. IIITs at Gwalior,\nKancheepuram, Jabalpur, Allahabad, Kottayam, Pune etc have established\ntechnology based incubation center to promote innovation and\nentrepreneurship in IT and its applicable areas.\n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |998", "t": "PSBs` Pensioners", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 998 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 8th FEBRUARY, 2021(MONDAY)/ MAGHA 19, 1942 (Saka) \nPSBs’ Pensioners \n \n998.  SHRI LAVU SRI KRISHNA DEVARAYALU: \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government proposes to issue administrative instructions to the Indian \nBanks Association to update the pension of retired employees of the Public Sector \nBanks (PSBs); \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government proposes to implement the One Rank One Pension \nprinciple for the retired PSBs‘ employees; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the time by which it is likely to be implemented? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE \n(SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR) \n(a) and (b):  Pension of pensioners of nationalised banks is financed by the respective \nbank out of its commercially generated revenues. Such pension was introduced as a \nfunded scheme on the basis of consensus arrived at b etween bank employee \nunions/associations and the Indian Banks’ Association (IBA), which negotiated on behalf \nof participating banks. The Boards of the respective nationalised bank accordingly made \nEmployees’ Pension Regulations in exercise of their powers under section 19 of the \nBanking Companies (Acquisition and Transfer of Undertakings) Act, 1970/1980 . IBA has \nrecently (on 25.1.2021) recommended that family pension be improved to 30% for all \nemployees without any cap, and the said recommendation is under consideration of the \nGovernment. \n(c): No proposal regarding implementation of One Rank One Pension is currently under \nconsideration of the Government. \n (d): Does not arise. \n*** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|5|UNSTARRED |999", "t": "Incentivizing Girl Students", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION\nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 999\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 08.02.2021\nIncentivizing Girl Students\n†999. SHRI AJAY KUMAR MISRA TENI\nWill the Minister of EDUCATION शिक् मंत् be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government is contemplating any scheme to incentivize girl students by\nproviding them scooter, cycle and financial allowance etc. through the State Governments\nwith the aim to ensure that they attend school/colleges regularly in the country;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor?\nA N S W E R\nMINISTER OF EDUCATION\n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL 'NISHANK')\n(a) to (c): Department of School Education and Literacy (DoSEL), Ministry of Education is\nimplementing Samagra Shiksha - an Integrated Scheme for School Education (ISSE). Under\nSamagra Shiksha, there is a provision of flexible funds for innovation for States and UTs which,\ninter-alia, can be used for transport and escort facility to children in Classes IX-XII in form of\nbus passes, cycles etc. Many of the States/UTs have implemented this option as an incentive to\nincrease enrolment especially for girls.\nUnder Samagra Shiksha, there is also a provision of annual stipend for girls belonging to\nCWSN(Chidren with Special Needs) @ Rs. 200 per month for 10 months.\nFurther, DoSEL, Ministry of Education is implementing a Central Sector Scheme\n‘National Means-cum-Merit Scholarship Scheme (NMMSS)’ since 2008 with the objective to\naward scholarships to meritorious students, including girls, of Economically Weaker Sections\n(EWS) to arrest their drop-out at class VIII and encourage them to continue the study at\nSecondary Stage. The scholarships are awarded to meritorious students, whose parental income\n\nfrom all sources is not more than Rs. 1,50,000/- per annum. Under the scheme, one lakh fresh\nscholarships of Rs.12000/- per annum per student are awarded to selected students of class IX\nevery year and are continued/renewed in classes X to XII for study in a State Government,\nGovernment-aided and Local body schools under the scheme. The scheme has helped in\nreducing the drop-out rate at the secondary and senior secondary classes.\nMoreover, the Central Sector Scheme of Scholarship for College and University\nStudents is being implemented since 2008 with the objective to provide financial assistance to\nthe meritorious students having family income of less than Rs. 8 lakh per annum, to meet a part\nof their day-to-day expenses while pursuing higher studies. The scholarships are awarded on the\nbasis of the results of Senior Secondary Examination. 50% of the scholarship is earmarked for\ngirls. The rate of the Scholarship is Rs. 10000/- per annum at Graduation level for the first three\nyears of College and University courses and Rs. 20000/- per annum at Post Graduation level.\nStudents pursuing professional course, in case, where the duration of course is five\nyears/integrated course would get Rs. 20000/- per annum in the 4th and 5th year.\n*****"}]}